COLLDATA("tadabburen","en",[[480,"§Fussilat\ndeeds\nGive a gift to someone with whom you have a misunderstanding, then watch how it softens your hearts.\nIf you are prompted by satan's provocation, seek refuge with Allah from him.\nProstrate after reading this verse.\nguid\nThe believer knows what will be his fate in the Hereafter when his soul leaves his body.\nIn Paradise, the believer will have therein whatever the souls desire and what delights the eyes.\nPractice patience; it is the best of all good manners.\nrefl\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ قَالُواْ رَبُّنَا ٱللَّهُ ثُمَّ ٱسۡتَقَٰمُواْ تَتَنَزَّلُ عَلَيۡهِمُ ٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ\nThis verse, (those who have said, \"Our Lord is Allah\" and then remained steadfast), combines the two fundamentals of Islamic perfection, where this part, (those who have said, \"Our Lord is Allah\") indicates mental perfection, which recognizing the truth in order to follow it and knowing what is good in order to practice it. This part, (and then remained steadfast) indicates the foundation of righteous deeds, which is standing firm on the right course. Ibn Ashur: 24/283.\nThis verse, (those who have said, \"Our Lord is Allah\" and then remained steadfast) combines the two fundamentals of human perfection. How?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ قَالُواْ رَبُّنَا ٱللَّهُ ثُمَّ ٱسۡتَقَٰمُواْ\nOmar bin Al-Khattab (t) said: \"Remaining steadfast is to adhere to what is commanded and what is prohibited, and not evade like a fox.\" Othman bin Affan (t) said: \"Those who sincerely devoted their deeds to Allah.\" Ali bin Abi Talib (t) said: \"Those who performed what is obligated.\" Al-Baghawi: 4/65-66.\nExplain the intended meaning of the reality of remaining steadfast in this verse.\nنَحۡنُ أَوۡلِيَآؤُكُمۡ فِي ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَفِي ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِۖ\nMeaning: The angels that descend upon them with good tidings, saying: (We are your allies). Mujahid said: It means that we are your associates who were with you in worldly life. On the Day of Resurrection, they will say: We will not part ways with you until we take you to Paradise. Al-Qurtubi: 18/418.\nThis verse describes a benefit for the believers from the world of angels. What is it?\nوَمَنْ أَحْسَنُ قَوۡلٗا مِّمَّن دَعَآ إِلَى ٱللَّهِ وَعَمِلَ صَٰلِحٗا وَقَالَ إِنَّنِي مِنَ ٱلۡمُسۡلِمِينَ ٣٣\nMeaning: He himself follows what he says, so it benefits him as well as others. He is not one of those who enjoin good but do not do it, or forbid evil yet they do it, rather, he does good and avoids doing evil, and he calls people to their Creator, the Almighty. Ibn Kathir: 4/102.\nThe truthful preacher has a sign. What is it?\nوَمَا يُلَقَّىٰهَآ إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ صَبَرُواْ وَمَا يُلَقَّىٰهَآ إِلَّا ذُو حَظٍّ عَظِيمٍ٣٥\nMeaning: No one is enabled to attain this good characteristic (except those who are patient), and make themselves endure with patience what they dislike, and force themselves to do what Allah loves. For people are naturally inclined to respond to mistreatment in like manner, and not to forgive, let alone react with kindness. But if a person makes himself to be patient and obeys the command of his Lord, while being aware of the immense reward that this attitude brings, understands that responding in kind to the one who mistreats him will not benefit him in the slightest and will only make the enmity worse. Moreover, treating him kindly will not detract from his status, for whoever humbles himself for the sake of Allah, Allah will raise him in rank, then kindness toward others will become easy for him and he will do it with pleasure and find delight in it. Al-Saadi: 749.\nThis status is granted to those who are patient and of a great portion of good. Why?\nوَمَا يُلَقَّىٰهَآ إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ صَبَرُواْ وَمَا يُلَقَّىٰهَآ إِلَّا ذُو حَظٍّ عَظِيمٍ٣٥\nSince it is one of the characteristics of the elite among humankind, by means of which a person attains high status in this world and the hereafter, it is one of the greatest of good characteristics. Al-Saadi: 749.\nThis verse describes a sign of a great characteristic of the elite among humankind to Allah. What is it?\nوَإِمَّا يَنْزَغَنَّكَ مِنَ الشَّيْطَانِ نَزْغٌ فَاسْتَعِذْ بِاللَّهِ إِنَّهُ هُوَ السَّمِيعُ الْعَلِيمُ٣٦\nAfter Allah mentioned how to respond to human enemies, which is by responding to maltreatment with kindness, Allah now teaches us how to ward off the jinn enemy, which is by seeking refuge and protection with Allah from his evil. (And if a prompting from satan stirs you up), any time you feel any of the promptings of satan - namely his whispers, making evil fair-seeming to you, discouraging you from doing good, tempting you to commit some sins or making you obey some of his instructions, (seek refuge with Allah), ask Him while expressing your need of Him to give you refuge and protect you from satan. Al-Saadi: 750.\nHow can we ward off the enemy from jinn?\nwords\nاستَقَامُواThey remained steadfast in truth by words and deeds\nوَلِيٌّ حَمِيمٌA devoted friend\nوَمَا يُلَقَّاهَاNone is enabled to attain it\nيَنزَغَنَّكَPrompted you\nفَاستَعِذ بِاللهِSeek refuge with Allah\nلاَ يَسأَمُونَThey never become weary"],[481,"§Fussilat\ndeeds\nAsk Allah to revive your heart with faith like He revives the dead earth with water.\nShare a message in which you give glad tidings that Allah's mercy is near, and all things will be all right.\nPlace your hand on the position of pain, then recite what you can from the Quran, as it is a cure.\nguid\nThe believer knows what will be his fate in the Hereafter when his soul leaves his body.\nThe doubts of the disbelievers, hypocrites and secularists about the Quran and religion are similar throughout the centuries.\nThe Quran is remedy and cure for those who have faith, and it is an affliction upon the disbelievers and hypocrites.\nrefl\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ يُلۡحِدُونَ فِيٓ ءَايَٰتِنَا لَا يَخۡفَوۡنَ عَلَيۡنَآۗ\nThis is a stern warning and dire threat, stating that He, may He be exalted, knows who denies His signs, Names and attributes, and He will punish them for that. Ibn Kathir: 4/104.\nAllah informs us that the deviators are not concealed from Him. Why?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ بِٱلذِّكۡرِ لَمَّا جَآءَهُمۡۖ وَإِنَّهُۥ لَكِتَٰبٌ عَزِيزٞ ٤١\nAllah describes His Book as (mighty) because the truth of its meanings makes it above and beyond any calumniation; moreover, it is preserved by Allah, the Almighty. Ibn Atiyah: 5/19.\nAllah describes the Quran as (mighty). Why?\nمَّا يُقَالُ لَكَ إِلَّا مَا قَدۡ قِيلَ لِلرُّسُلِ مِن قَبۡلِكَۚ إِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَذُو مَغۡفِرَةٖ وَذُو عِقَابٍ أَلِيمٖ ٤٣\nDescribing the punishment as severe is befitting to what they had committed because they caused severe pain to the Prophet’s (ﷺ) soul by their denial and annoyance. Ibn Ashur: 24/311.\nThe punishment is described as severe. Why?\nإِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَذُو مَغۡفِرَةٖ وَذُو عِقَابٍ أَلِيمٖ ٤٣\nIf it was not for Allah's forgiveness, no one would be have been able to enjoy life; and if it was not for His warning and punishment, everyone would become careless. Ibn Kathir: 4/104.\nSimilar to this verse, many verses in the Quran combine forgiveness and punishment. Why?\nقُلۡ هُوَ لِلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ هُدٗى وَشِفَآءٞۚ\nKnow that the Quran is a guidance and a cure from doubt and ailments for all those who believe in it. Al-Qurtubi: 18/431.\nWho benefits from the Quran's guidance and cure?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ لَا يُؤۡمِنُونَ فِيٓ ءَاذَانِهِمۡ وَقۡرٞ وَهُوَ عَلَيۡهِمۡ عَمًىۚ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ يُنَادَوۡنَ مِن مَّكَانِۢ بَعِيدٖ ٤٤\nMeaning: They do not listen, nor understand, similar to someone who is called from a distant place where he does not hear nor understand. This is an example of their lack of benefit from admonishments, where they are called from that which they cannot hear. Al-Baghawi: 4/70.\nWhat is meant by this Quranic example, (Those are being called from a distant place)?\nوَلَقَدۡ ءَاتَيۡنَا مُوسَى ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ فَٱخۡتُلِفَ فِيهِۚ وَلَوۡلَا كَلِمَةٞ سَبَقَتۡ مِن رَّبِّكَ لَقُضِيَ بَيۡنَهُمۡۚ وَإِنَّهُمۡ لَفِي شَكّٖ مِّنۡهُ مُرِيبٖ ٤٥\nAllah says: The false group among them were (in doubt) of what they had said about the Quran. (Disquieting), they were disquieted by what they said because they were not convinced of their saying but only assumed. Al-Tabari: 21/487.\nThe disbelievers were not convinced of what they said about the Quran. Why?\nwords\nاهتَزَّتIt quivers and grows plants\nوَرَبَتIt swells\nيُلحِدُونَThey deviate from the truth\nوَقرٌDeafness\nمُرِيبٍA disquieting doubt"],[482,"§Fussilat\ndeeds\nAsk Allah to give you from His great bounty, and to teach you useful knowledge.\nRead some Quranic verses and Prophetic Hadiths about the Hour.\nAsk Allah to relieve your distress.\nguid\nOn the Day of Resurrection, every worshiper will part ways with those whom he used to worship, and each will disown the other.\nMan is weak, even in his mind and perceptions.\nWithout faith, man is the most misguided among all creatures.\nrefl\nلَّا يَسۡـَٔمُ ٱلۡإِنسَٰنُ مِن دُعَآءِ ٱلۡخَيۡرِ وَإِن مَّسَّهُ ٱلشَّرُّ فَيَـُٔوسٞ قَنُوطٞ ٤٩\nAllah reveals the nature of man and that he has no patience to deal with either times of ease or times of hardship, except those whom Allah helps to attain perfection. Al-Saadi: 752.\nYour body and heart are vulnerable. Explain this fact and its remedy in light of this verse.\nلَّا يَسۡـَٔمُ ٱلۡإِنسَٰنُ مِن دُعَآءِ ٱلۡخَيۡرِ وَإِن مَّسَّهُ ٱلشَّرُّ فَيَـُٔوسٞ قَنُوطٞ ٤٩ وَلَئِنۡ أَذَقۡنَٰهُ رَحۡمَةٗ مِّنَّا مِنۢ بَعۡدِ ضَرَّآءَ مَسَّتۡهُ لَيَقُولَنَّ هَٰذَا لِي وَمَآ أَظُنُّ ٱلسَّاعَةَ قَآئِمَةٗ وَلَئِن رُّجِعۡتُ إِلَىٰ رَبِّيٓ إِنَّ لِي عِندَهُۥ لَلۡحُسۡنَىٰۚ\nMan is described by two dreadful traits: When touched by evil, he becomes despairing and despondent; and when good fortune comes his way, he forgets that Allah is the Bestower, and becomes insolent, believing that he deserved this good fortune. Moreover, he denies the resurrection (and I do not think the Hour will occur), adding his false premise that if he is resurrected, he will receive the best from his Lord. Surely, this leaves no more room for ignorance and conceit. Ibn Al-Qayim: 2/420.\nWhat are the two dreadful traits that one can have when touched by evil and good fortune?\nوَإِذَآ أَنۡعَمۡنَا عَلَى ٱلۡإِنسَٰنِ أَعۡرَضَ وَنَـَٔا بِجَانِبِهِۦ وَإِذَا مَسَّهُ ٱلشَّرُّ فَذُو دُعَآءٍ عَرِيضٍ ٥١\n(He is full of extensive supplication): Because he has no patience, he does not show patience during times of hardship and does not show gratitude during times of ease, except those whom Allah guides and blesses. Al-Saadi: 752\nHow should the believer react during times of affliction and prosperity?\nوَإِذَآ أَنۡعَمۡنَا عَلَى ٱلۡإِنسَٰنِ أَعۡرَضَ وَنَـَٔا بِجَانِبِهِۦ وَإِذَا مَسَّهُ ٱلشَّرُّ فَذُو دُعَآءٍ عَرِيضٍ ٥١\nThe Quran teaches us to venerate Allah by not attributing evil to Him, as Abraham said, (Who created me, so He guides me), until he said, (and when I am ill He heals me) [26:78-80]. He did not say, \"When He makes me ill\", and there is a secret to this, which is that blessings and good fortune are subjected to man in the essence of his creation, and they are mostly in his life because they maintain his survival. Evil and afflictions befall him mostly due to his misdeeds and transgressions against the limits that divine Sharias and wise men [Prophets] warned him against; hence, he seldom falls into them except by his knowledge and audacity. Ibn Ashur: 25/15.\nThe verse does not attribute evil to Allah. Why? How does evil afflict man?\nسَنُرِيهِمۡ ءَايَٰتِنَا فِي ٱلۡأٓفَاقِ وَفِيٓ أَنفُسِهِمۡ حَتَّىٰ يَتَبَيَّنَ لَهُمۡ أَنَّهُ ٱلۡحَقُّ\nMeaning: The Quran is true, and Allah makes clear that He will definitely show them some of His witnessed signs to prove the trueness of His recited verses. Ibn Al-Qayim: 2/420.\nAllah's signs in the universe and within the soul prove the trueness of the Quran. Explain in light of this verse.\nسَنُرِيهِمۡ ءَايَٰتِنَا فِي ٱلۡأٓفَاقِ وَفِيٓ أَنفُسِهِمۡ حَتَّىٰ يَتَبَيَّنَ لَهُمۡ أَنَّهُ ٱلۡحَقُّ\nPart of the inimitable nature of the Quran is relating things from the unseen, as this verse reveals. It informs about the promise of victory of this religion through Allah's empowerment of His Messenger (ﷺ) and his Caliphs afterward in conquering the east and west of the land. Despite its small size army, the Muslim nation’s stability and influence on others, the likes of which had never been attained by kings, Caesars, or emperors. The spreading of Muslims and their dominance over other nations was historically unprecedented, which indicates that Islam is the truth and that when Muslims adhere to its principles, they receive Allah's victory in a remarkable way. The former and latter people attest to this fact. Ibn Ashur: 25/18.\nThis verse relates an inimitable news from the unseen. Explain.\nأَلَآ إِنَّهُمۡ فِي فِي مِرۡيَةٖ مِّن لِّقَآءِ رَبِّهِمۡۗ\nOmar bin Abdulaziz (t) ascended the pulpit and praised Allah, then said: \"O people, I did not gather you to originate something, but I have thought about the end that all people are going to meet. I came to realize that the one who believes this meeting is a fool, and the one who denies it is doomed.\" Then, he came down from the pulpit. The meaning of \"the one who believes this meeting is a fool\" is that he does not do good deeds, nor does he fear its terror, even though he believes in it and is sure of its occurrence. However, despite all that, he persists in his diversion, heedlessness, and sins hence, he is a fool in this regard, and, linguistically speaking, a fool is defined as a weak-minded person. Ibn Kathir: 4/107.\nThe actions of some of those who believe in the Day of Resurrection reflect that they are in doubt about it. Explain.\nwords\nأَكمَامِهَاHusk\nآذَنَّاكَWe announce to You\nمَحِيصٍEscape\nلاَ يَسأَمُHe is not weary\nوَنَأَى بِجَانِبِهِHe distances himself from following the truth\nفَذُو دُعَاءٍ عَرِيضٍHe is full of extensive supplication\nشِقَاقٍExtreme dissension"],[483,"§Ash-Shura\ndeeds\nFollowing the example of the angels, ask for Allah’s forgiveness for yourself and all the believers, males and females, on earth.\nExhort the people in the mosque, or share a message about the Day of Resurrection.\nLook up an issue about which those around have differed, search for Allah’s ruling concerning it, and remind them of it.\nguid\nThe believer shares his brethren's burden of distress.\nThe Holy Quran is the best source for admonishments and lessons.\nArabic language will remain the key to learning the right religion, so, ensure to learn it.\nrefl\nكَذَٰلِكَ يُوحِيٓ إِلَيۡكَ وَإِلَى ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبۡلِكَ ٱللَّهُ ٱلۡعَزِيزُ ٱلۡحَكِيمُ ٣\nThese two attributes of Allah (the Al-Mighty, the All-Wise) are mentioned because their meanings pertain to the intended objective, which is that Allah chooses whomever He Wills for His revelation. Ibn Ashur: 25/27.\nThis verse ends with the attributes of Allah (the Al-Mighty, the All-Wise). Why?\nتَكَادُ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتُ يَتَفَطَّرۡنَ مِن فَوۡقِهِنَّۚ\nMeaning: Each one of them almost burst apart on top of the one below it due to the saying of the polytheists: (And they say, \"Allah has taken a son\") [2:116]. Al-Qurtubi: 18/444.\nWhat is the reason that the heavens almost burst apart?\nتَكَادُ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتُ يَتَفَطَّرۡنَ مِن فَوۡقِهِنَّۚ وَٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ يُسَبِّحُونَ بِحَمۡدِ رَبِّهِمۡ\nGlorifying Allah precedes praising Him to indicate that exalting Allah above all deficiencies is more important than affirming His perfect attributes because the exaltation of Allah is a prelude to His perfect attributes. Ibn Ashur: 25/33.\nGlorifying Allah precedes praising Him. Why?\nوَٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ يُسَبِّحُونَ بِحَمۡدِ رَبِّهِمۡ وَيَسۡتَغۡفِرُونَ لِمَن فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِۗ\nThey ask their Lord's forgiveness for the sins of the believers on earth. Al-Tabari: 21/502.\nThe closest beings to Allah are those who are most merciful toward other beings. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَمَا ٱخۡتَلَفۡتُمۡ فِيهِ مِن شَيۡءٖ فَحُكۡمُهُۥٓ إِلَى ٱللَّهِۚ\nWhat this verse implies is that the agreement of the Ummah constitutes definitive proof, because Allah did not instruct us to refer to Him except concerning that in which we differ. As for that on which we agreed, the unanimous agreement of the Ummah is sufficient proof, because the Ummah as a whole is infallible and cannot agree upon error; its consensus must be in agreement with what is in the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of His Messenger (ﷺ). Al-Saadi: 753.\nHow does this verse imply that the consensus of the Ummah constitutes definitive proof?\nعَلَيۡهِ تَوَكَّلۡتُ وَإِلَيۡهِ أُنِيبُ ١٠\nAllah often mentions these two principles (trusting Allah and turning to Him) in His Book because with both of them together one may attain perfection that is not possible without them or without one of them, such as in the verses in which He says: (You [Alone] we worship, and You [Alone] we ask for help) [1:5], and (So worship Him [alone] and put your trust in Him) [11:123]. Al-Saadi: 754.\nIn the Book of Allah, trusting Allah and worshiping Him are often mentioned together. Why?\nذَٰلِكُمُ ٱللَّهُ رَبِّي عَلَيۡهِ تَوَكَّلۡتُ وَإِلَيۡهِ أُنِيبُ ١٠\nThe verb in this phrase, (I have relied) is in the past tense form to indicate that his reliance on his Lord before encountering his people's denial, thus, they faced a servant who was reliant on his Lord. The verb in the next phrase (I turn back) is in the present tense to indicate his repeated return to his Lord. Ibn Ashur: 25/43.\nThe verb in (I have relied) is in the past tense, and the verb in (I turn back) is in the present tense. Why?\nwords\nيَتَفَطَّرنَBurst apart\nأَولِيَاءَGods, they worshiped\nحَفِيظٌWatchful over them\nأُمَّ القُرَىMakkah, warning to its inhabitants\nلاَ رَيبَ فِيهِAbout which there is no doubt\nأُمَّةً وَاحِدَةًAll of them belong to one religion\nوَإِلَيهِ أُنِيبُTo Him I turn back on all matters"],[484,"§Ash-Shura\ndeeds\nInvite a friend or relative to join you in doing an act of worship or sunnah.\nFollowing Allah's commands, say this sentence:\nLook for a religious innovation (bid'a) or a sin that has spread around you, keep away from it, and spread awareness about it.\nguid\nAffirming the attributes of Allah, the Almighty, and negating His likeness to the created beings.\nBe content with what Allah has given you, for He is the one Who extends and restricts provision.\nGood intentions and diligence in seeking guidance are among the reasons for its attainment.\nrefl\n۞شَرَعَ لَكُم مِّنَ ٱلدِّينِ مَا وَصَّىٰ بِهِۦ نُوحٗا وَٱلَّذِيٓ أَوۡحَيۡنَآ إِلَيۡكَ وَمَا وَصَّيۡنَا بِهِۦٓ إِبۡرَٰهِيمَ وَمُوسَىٰ وَعِيسَىٰٓۖ\nThis is the greatest blessing that Allah has bestowed upon His servants, that He has prescribed for them the best and purest of religions, namely the religion of Islam, which Allah has prescribed for the chosen ones among His servants. Indeed, Allah prescribed it for the best of the best, the elite of the elite, namely the Messengers of firm resolve who are mentioned in this verse, who are the highest of humankind in status and the most perfect in all aspects. Al-Saadi: 754.\nWhat is Allah's greatest blessing upon you?\n۞شَرَعَ لَكُم مِّنَ ٱلدِّينِ مَا وَصَّىٰ بِهِۦ نُوحٗا وَٱلَّذِيٓ أَوۡحَيۡنَآ إِلَيۡكَ وَمَا وَصَّيۡنَا بِهِۦٓ إِبۡرَٰهِيمَ وَمُوسَىٰ وَعِيسَىٰٓۖ أَنۡ أَقِيمُواْ ٱلدِّينَ وَلَا تَتَفَرَّقُواْ فِيهِۚ\nThe religion of our Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ) is in accordance with all the prophets in the fundamentals of faith, that is the meaning of this verse. Hence, Allah explains it by saying, (to establish the religion), which means Islam, the Oneness of Allah, obedience to Him, believing in His Messengers, Books, and the Hereafter. As for the minor rulings, each Sharia has its own, and that is not what is meant by this verse. Ibn Juzay: 2/299.\nWhat are the things that the Prophets' Messages have in common? What are the things that they differ about?\nأَنۡ أَقِيمُواْ ٱلدِّينَ وَلَا تَتَفَرَّقُواْ فِيهِۚ\nAllah has sent all the Prophets to establish religion, harmony, and unity, and discard division and discord. Al-Baghawi: 4/77.\nThis verse presents a common objective with which all Prophets were sent. What is it?\nكَبُرَ عَلَى ٱلۡمُشۡرِكِينَ مَا تَدۡعُوهُمۡ إِلَيۡهِۚ\nMeaning: It is hard for them (that to which you invite them), which is the Oneness of Allah and rejection of idols. Qatadah said: Testifying to the Oneness of Allah was difficult for the polytheists, and Iblees and his soldiers were distressed because of it, but Allah refused except to raise it high and empower it over those who opposed it. Al-Qurtubi: 18/453.\nThe polytheists faced a difficult matter. What was it?\nوَمَا تَفَرَّقُوٓاْ إِلَّا مِنۢ بَعۡدِ مَا جَآءَهُمُ ٱلۡعِلۡمُ بَغۡيَۢا بَيۡنَهُمۡۚ\nThe division among them was not due to unclarity of proof, rather, the animosity between them was due to fighting over headship, transgression, and pursing worldly gains. Al-Qurtubi: 18/454.\nWhat is the reason for the division among eminent Muslims despite the availability of knowledge?\nوَمَا تَفَرَّقُوٓاْ إِلَّا مِنۢ بَعۡدِ مَا جَآءَهُمُ ٱلۡعِلۡمُ\nHaving commanded the Muslims to be united in their religion, and forbidden them from being divided, Allah informs them that they should not take it for granted that they will remain united just because Allah has sent down the Book to them, for the People of the Book did not become divided until Allah sent down to them the Book that required them to be united. Al-Saadi: 755.\nWhat is the useful lesson that we draw from being informed about the people of the Book?\nوَلَا تَتَّبِعۡ أَهۡوَآءَهُمۡۖ\nAllah did not say \"do not follow their religion\" because their original religion, which Allah had prescribed for them, was the religion of all the Messengers, but they did not follow it; rather they followed their whims and desires and they took their religion as a mockery and a mere game. Al-Saadi: 755.\nThis verse cautions against the risk of innovation in religion. Explain.\nwords\nفَاطِرُThe Originator, Creator\nيَذرَؤُكُم فِيهِHe causes you to multiply in number\nمَقَالِيدُ السَّمَاوَاتِThe keys of the heavens\nيَبسُطُHe extends\nوَيَقدِرُHe restricts\nيَجتَبِي إِلَيهِHe chooses for His Oneness and religion\nيُنِيبُTurns back in obedience\nمُرِيبٍA disquieting doubt"],[485,"§Ash-Shura\ndeeds\nDo a good deed that reflects your faith that the Hour is near.\nThink about yourself and record three aspects of Allah’s kindness toward you.\nPlant a wish in your heart for a great righteous deed, and strive to achieve it, so Allah may give more righteous deeds.\nguid\nClarifying some of the wisdom behind sending down the Book, which is the Quran, and justice by which people rule and judge.\nIt is important to maintain good intentions, as the acceptance or rejection of the deed is based on it.\nBeware of religious inventions, for they are among the reasons for the deviation of former religions. They bring Allah's wrath, hence, the devil does not discourage the servant from doing them.\nrefl\nٱللَّهُ ٱلَّذِيٓ أَنزَلَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ بِٱلۡحَقِّ وَٱلۡمِيزَانَۗ وَمَا يُدۡرِيكَ لَعَلَّ ٱلسَّاعَةَ قَرِيبٞ ١٧\nIf someone asks: What is the link between mentioning the Hour with the Book and justice? The answer is: The Hour will be the Day of Recompense and Account. It is as if saying: Be just and do the right thing before the Day on which you will be held accountable for your deeds. Ibn Juzay: 2/300.\nThe mention the Hour comes after the Book and justice. Why?\nيَسۡتَعۡجِلُ بِهَا ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يُؤۡمِنُونَ بِهَاۖ وَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ مُشۡفِقُونَ مِنۡهَا\nMeaning: They are afraid because of their belief in it and their knowledge of what it will involve of requital for deeds. Their fear is due to their knowledge of their Lord, for they fear that their deeds will not save them or lead them to a place of happiness. Al-Saadi: 756.\nThe believers are fearful of the Hour. Why?\nٱللَّهُ لَطِيفُۢ بِعِبَادِهِۦ يَرۡزُقُ مَن يَشَآءُۖ\nAnother aspect of His kindness is that He has provided to His servant every means that may form a barrier between him and sins, to the extent that if Allah knows that worldly gain, wealth, headship and other things for which people compete in this world could cause His servant to turn away from obedience to Him, or make him negligent or lead him into sin, He diverts it from him and restricts his provision. Hence, He says here: (He gives provision to whom He wills). Al-Saadi: 757.\nAllah mentions His giving of provision after His kindness to His servants. Why?\nٱللَّهُ لَطِيفُۢ بِعِبَادِهِۦ يَرۡزُقُ مَن يَشَآءُۖ وَهُوَ ٱلۡقَوِيُّ ٱلۡعَزِيزُ ١٩\nThese two attributes: (The All-Powerful, the All-Mighty) are exaltation of Allah, and are mentioned right after the attribute of (Kind), or after this sentence, (He gives provision to whom He wills) to safeguard against giving the wrong impression to one who may misunderstand that Allah’s Kindness is out of weakness or persuasion, or that giving provision to whom He wills may be construed as stinginess or deficiency. Rather, He is not weak nor does He need to persuade anyone; He is the All-Powerful, hence, there are no causes for stinginess, and He is the All-Mighty, hence, there is no cause for poverty. His specific provision to whom He wills is based on His wisdom of knowing the states (general and specific) of His servants. Ibn Ashur: 25/73.\n(The All-Powerful, the All-Mighty) are mentioned right after the attribute of (Kind). Why?\nٱللَّهُ لَطِيفُۢ بِعِبَادِهِۦ يَرۡزُقُ مَن يَشَآءُۖ وَهُوَ ٱلۡقَوِيُّ ٱلۡعَزِيزُ ١٩\nMuhammad bin Ali Al-Kattani said: He is kind to those of His servants who seek refuge with Him, when they despair of others, rely, and return to Him, then Allah will turn to them and accept them. Other interpretations are listed here: The One Who spreads the good deeds of His servants and hides their faults. The One Who accepts the small deeds and gives plenitude. The One Who mends the broken hearts and relieves the hardship. The One Who does not haste to punish those who disobey Him, nor does He disappoint those who hope for His mercy. The One Who answers those who supplicate Him, and does not despair those who seek Him. The One Who forgives those who slip. The One Who is merciful toward those who are not merciful to themselves. Al-Qurtubi: 18/459-461\nWhat do you know about the kindness of Allah?\nمَن كَانَ يُرِيدُ حَرۡثَ ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ نَزِدۡ لَهُۥ فِي حَرۡثِهِۦۖ\nMeaning: Whoever sought the reward of the Hereafter through using the provision We provided for Him by giving others what is rightfully theirs, and spending in support of the religion, We Will reward him ten to seven hundred times and more for what he spent. Al-Qurtubi: 18/461.\nWhat is meant by (We will increase for him his harvest)?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ فِي رَوۡضَاتِ ٱلۡجَنَّاتِۖ لَهُم مَّا يَشَآءُونَ عِندَ رَبِّهِمۡۚ ذَٰلِكَ هُوَ ٱلۡفَضۡلُ ٱلۡكَبِيرُ ٢٢\nOne of the subtleties of this description is that it comes in accordance with the familiar order of things. When a guest arrives, first, he is provided with a good place to rest, then food and drinks are brought to him, then, the host gets nearer and mixes with him. Ibn Ashur: 25/79.\nThis verse describes three stages of hospitality for the believers in Paradise. Explain.\nwords\nيُحَآجُّونَ فِي اللهِThose who argue about the religion of Allah\nدَاحِضَةٌInvalid, false\nمُشفِقُونَ مِنهَاThey are fearful of it\nيُمَارُونَThose who dispute\nحَرثَ الآخِرَةِIts reward\nكَلِمَةُ الفَصلِHis decree of giving them respite"],[486,"§Ash-Shura\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, accept my repentance and forgive my sins.\"\nRespond to one of Allah's commands mentioned in the verses, so that Allah increases His bounty upon you.\nRecall a calamity that befell you, then ask often for Allah's forgiveness while remembering the words of the Almighty.\nguid\nAllah's promise of eliminating falsehood is indeed true.\nDistributing livelihoods among the creation is in accordance with Allah's wisdom.\nOne of the signs of Allah's mercy toward His creation is sending down the rain, which is a blessing that warrants gratefulness.\nrefl\nذَٰلِكَ ٱلَّذِي يُبَشِّرُ ٱللَّهُ عِبَادَهُ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِۗ\nHaving mentioned the gardens of Paradise, Allah then says to His servants who believe and do righteous deeds: (That is the glad tidings that Allah gives to His servants who believe and do righteous deeds) meaning, this will undoubtedly come to them, because it is glad tidings from Allah to them. Ibn Kathir: 4/114.\nWhat is the purpose of glad tidings to the believers in this verse?\nوَهُوَ ٱلَّذِي يَقۡبَلُ ٱلتَّوۡبَةَ عَنۡ عِبَادِهِۦ وَيَعۡفُواْ عَنِ ٱلسَّيِّـَٔاتِ وَيَعۡلَمُ مَا تَفۡعَلُونَ ٢٥\nBecause repentance is one of the great deeds that may be perfected because of complete sincerity and resolve, or it may be imperfect if sincerity is lacking, or it may be invalid if the aim is to attain some worldly gain, and because the place of repentance is the heart, which no one knows except Allah, He concludes this verse with the words: (And He knows what you do). Al-Saadi: 758.\nThe verse ends with: (And He knows what you do). Why?\nوَهُوَ ٱلَّذِي يَقۡبَلُ ٱلتَّوۡبَةَ عَنۡ عِبَادِهِۦ وَيَعۡفُواْ عَنِ ٱلسَّيِّـَٔاتِ وَيَعۡلَمُ مَا تَفۡعَلُونَ ٢٥\nThe use of the term: (His servants) instead of “the people”, or “the repentant”, points to the fact that Allah is Forbearer toward His servants because of their submissiveness to Him, as the creator likes the best for its creation. Ibn Ashur: 25/90.\nIn this verse, why is the term: (His servants) used instead of the people, or the repentant?\n۞وَلَوۡ بَسَطَ ٱللَّهُ ٱلرِّزۡقَ لِعِبَادِهِۦ لَبَغَوۡاْ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَلَٰكِن يُنَزِّلُ بِقَدَرٖ مَّا يَشَآءُۚ إِنَّهُۥ بِعِبَادِهِۦ خَبِيرُۢ بَصِيرٞ ٢٧\nAllah may know that when He extends His provision to one of His servants, it will lead him to corruption; therefore, in the interest of His servant, Allah withholds some worldly gains from him. So, the restriction of provision does not mean humiliation, nor does its extension mean honor. It is narrated that Allah says, \"There are some among my believing servants who ask Me for a certain act of worship that I know if I give that to him, he will be boastful. There are some among my believing servants whose affairs can be set in order only when he is prosperous, and if I restrict his provision, he will become corrupt. There are some among my believing servants whose affairs can be set in order only when he is indigent, and if I extend his provision, he will become corrupt.\" Al-Qurtubi: 18/475.\nIs the extension of provision good for man at all times?\nوَهُوَ ٱلَّذِي يُنَزِّلُ ٱلۡغَيۡثَ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ مَا قَنَطُواْ وَيَنشُرُ رَحۡمَتَهُۥۚ وَهُوَ ٱلۡوَلِيُّ ٱلۡحَمِيدُ ٢٨\nAmong worldly blessings, sending down the rain is singled out for mention because there is no dispute among people that it is the basis for the continuation of life by providing sustenance for people and other creatures. Ibn Ashur: 25/95.\nAfter mentioning the general provision, sending down the rain is singled out for mention. Why?\nوَهُوَ ٱلَّذِي يُنَزِّلُ ٱلۡغَيۡثَ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ مَا قَنَطُواْ وَيَنشُرُ رَحۡمَتَهُۥۚ وَهُوَ ٱلۡوَلِيُّ ٱلۡحَمِيدُ ٢٨\nThese two attributes: (The Guardian, the Praiseworthy) are mentioned because they are suited to the subject of providing relief to people, where (the Guardian) is kind to those whom he guards, and (the Praiseworthy) gives that which he is praised for. Ibn Ashur: 25/96.\nThe attributes, (the Guardian, the Praiseworthy) are suited for the subject here. Explain.\nوَمَآ أَصَٰبَكُم مِّن مُّصِيبَةٖ فَبِمَا كَسَبَتۡ أَيۡدِيكُمۡ وَيَعۡفُواْ عَن كَثِيرٖ ٣٠\nMeaning: The afflictions that befall people's bodies and wealth are due to their sins. Ibn Juzay: 2/303.\nWhat do think about those who say that calamities have natural reasons, and that sins are not part of that?\nwords\nإِلاَّ المَوَدَّةَ فِي القُربَىKindness toward me because of our kinship\nيَقتَرِف حَسَنَةًCommits a good deed\nافتَرَىHe fabricated\nقَنَطُواThey had despaired of its coming\nوَيَنشُرُ رَحمَتَهُHe spreads His mercy\nبَثَّHe dispersed\nدَآبَّةٍA creature on earth, man and animal, etc."],[487,"§Ash-Shura\ndeeds\nWatch the ships as they sail the sea, or look at a picture of them, then record your observations so that you fulfill the reflection on this verse.\nWhen you hear the call for Prayer, drop everything and go to the mosque.\nConsult a friend on how best you can memorize a Surah from the Holy Quran.\nguid\nBeware of major sins.\nThe fact that the reward for pardon is with Allah is indicative of its great status.\nGuidance and misguidance are in the Hand of Allah, so ask Him to keep you firm on His religion.\nrefl\nوَمِنۡ ءَايَٰتِهِ ٱلۡجَوَارِ فِي ٱلۡبَحۡرِ كَٱلۡأَعۡلَٰمِ ٣٢ إِن يَشَأۡ يُسۡكِنِ ٱلرِّيحَ فَيَظۡلَلۡنَ رَوَاكِدَ عَلَىٰ ظَهۡرِهِۦٓۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّكُلِّ صَبَّارٖ شَكُورٍ ٣٣\nThe sailing ships are made a sign for (everyone who is steadfast and grateful) because for both cases [steadfastness and gratefulness] there is fear and safety, where fear entails steadfastness and safety entails gratefulness. Ibn Ashur: 25/106.\nThere is a sign for the steadfast and grateful in the sailing of the ships or being motionless at sea. Why?\nوَإِذَا مَا غَضِبُواْ هُمۡ يَغۡفِرُونَ ٣٧ وَٱلَّذِينَ إِذَآ أَصَابَهُمُ ٱلۡبَغۡيُ هُمۡ يَنتَصِرُونَ ٣٩\nEach account has its own appropriate place where it is praised. Pardoning the helpless who admits his fault is a praised action, and the term (forgive) implies it. Retaliation against the opponent who persists in his fault is a praised action, and the term (retaliate) implies it. If these two actions are reversed, they will be denounced, as an Arab poet said: If you honor the noble one, you gain his loyalty v but if you honor the ignoble, he will bite you. Using leniency when force is needed is harmful v just as using force when leniency is needed. Al-Alusi: 25/66.\nHow do we reconcile these verses, (And when they are angered, they forgive) and (And those who retaliate fairly when oppressed)?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ ٱسۡتَجَابُواْ لِرَبِّهِمۡ وَأَقَامُواْ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَأَمۡرُهُمۡ شُورَىٰ بَيۡنَهُمۡ وَمِمَّا رَزَقۡنَٰهُمۡ يُنفِقُونَ ٣٨\nPart of responding to Allah is establishing prayer and giving zakah, therefore they are mentioned after that, by way of following the mention of something in general terms with something specific, which is indicative of its importance and virtue. Al-Saadi: 760.\nEstablishing prayer and giving zakah are included within their response to Allah. Why are they mentioned afterward?\nوَأَمۡرُهُمۡ شُورَىٰ بَيۡنَهُمۡ\nMeaning: No one forces his own view with regard to any matter of their common affairs. This can only be a sign of their unity, harmony, mutual love, and perfect mature thinking. When they want to do something that requires discussion and exchange of views, they get together and discuss and examine the issue. Then, once it becomes clear to them what is the best option that will serve the interests of the community, they hasten to take a decision concerning that option. Al-Saadi: 760.\nMutual consultation among Muslims indicates another great matter. What is it?\nوَجَزَٰٓؤُاْ سَيِّئَةٖ سَيِّئَةٞ مِّثۡلُهَاۖ فَمَنۡ عَفَا وَأَصۡلَحَ فَأَجۡرُهُۥ عَلَى ٱللَّهِۚ\nPardon means forgiving and reconciling with the person who did wrong. Hence Allah says: (But whoever pardons and makes reconciliation, his reward is with Allah), so, Allah will reward him greatly and abundantly. But if the offender does not deserve to be forgiven and there is a Sharia interest to be served by punishing him, then in that case he is not enjoined to pardon him. Al-Saadi: 760.\nMaking reconciliation is mentioned after pardoning. Why?\nوَجَزَٰٓؤُاْ سَيِّئَةٖ سَيِّئَةٞ مِّثۡلُهَاۖ فَمَنۡ عَفَا وَأَصۡلَحَ فَأَجۡرُهُۥ عَلَى ٱللَّهِۚ\nStating that the reward of the one who forgives is with Allah motivates him to forgive and to treat others as he wants Allah to treat him. Just as he wants Allah to forgive him, let him forgive others, and just as he wants Allah to pardon him, let him pardon others, for the requital matches the deed. Al-Saadi: 760.\nThe reward for pardon is with Allah. What do we benefit from this fact?\nوَجَزَٰٓؤُاْ سَيِّئَةٖ سَيِّئَةٞ مِّثۡلُهَاۖ فَمَنۡ عَفَا وَأَصۡلَحَ فَأَجۡرُهُۥ عَلَى ٱللَّهِۚ إِنَّهُۥ لَا يُحِبُّ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٤٠ وَلَمَنِ ٱنتَصَرَ بَعۡدَ ظُلۡمِهِۦ فَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ مَا عَلَيۡهِم مِّن سَبِيلٍ ٤١\n(But whoever pardons and seeks reconciliation, his reward is with Allah), this indicates that pardoning transgressors is better than retaliation because the reward is mentioned for pardon while retaliation is mentioned as a permitted option, (whoever retaliates after being wronged, there is no blame on them). Ibn Juzay: 2/305.\nPardon is better than retaliation. How?\nwords\nالجَوَارِSailing ships\nكَالأَعلاَمِLike mountains\nرَوَاكِدَMotionless\nيُوبِقهُنَّHe capsizes them\nمَحِيصٍPlace of escape\nالبَغيُTransgression\nعَزمِ الأُمُورِMatters of great resolve"],[488,"§Ash-Shura\ndeeds\nRespond to every command and prohibition from Allah.\nAdvise your family and supplicate Allah for their guidance.\nLook for a verse with a command or a Prophetic Hadith of which you were hesitant to apply, and hasten to do it.\nguid\nWhat a great loss it will be for the transgressor on the Day of Resurrection!\nThe Messengers' mission is to convey and preach the Message.\nGranting offspring to the servants is in accordance with Allah's wisdom.\nrefl\nوَتَرَىٰهُمۡ يُعۡرَضُونَ عَلَيۡهَا خَٰشِعِينَ مِنَ ٱلذُّلِّ\nMeaning: Humiliation will overcome them, because of their previous disobedience toward Allah. Ibn Kathir: 4/122.\nWhat is the reason for their humiliation on the Day of Resurrection?\nوَقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِنَّ ٱلۡخَٰسِرِينَ ٱلَّذِينَ خَسِرُوٓاْ أَنفُسَهُمۡ وَأَهۡلِيهِمۡ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِۗ أَلَآ إِنَّ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ فِي عَذَابٖ مُّقِيمٖ ٤٥\nThey will lose themselves when they enter the Fire in which they will be tormented; and they will lose their families because if they are in the Fire, they will be of no benefit to them, and if they are in Paradise, a barrier will be set between them. Al-Shawkani: 4/543.\nHow will they lose themselves and families on the Day of Resurrection?\nٱسۡتَجِيبُواْ لِرَبِّكُم مِّن قَبۡلِ أَن يَأۡتِيَ يَوۡمٞ لَّا مَرَدَّ لَهُۥ مِنَ ٱللَّهِۚ مَا لَكُم مِّن مَّلۡجَإٖ يَوۡمَئِذٖ وَمَا لَكُم مِّن نَّكِيرٖ ٤٧\nIn this and similar verses, there is a condemnation of those who hope to live long and a command to make the most of any opportunity that comes along to do a good deed, because procrastinating leads to a great deal of trouble. Al-Saadi: 761.\nWhat is false hope? Is procrastinating good deeds justified?\nفَإِنۡ أَعۡرَضُواْ فَمَآ أَرۡسَلۡنَٰكَ عَلَيۡهِمۡ حَفِيظًاۖ\nMeaning: A keeper of their deeds so you call them to account. It is said that it means as a manager over them and bound to them until they believe, which means you cannot force them to believe. Al-Qurtubi: 18/500.\nThis verse consoles preachers to Allah when they get no response from others. Explain.\nوَإِنَّآ إِذَآ أَذَقۡنَا ٱلۡإِنسَٰنَ مِنَّا رَحۡمَةٗ فَرِحَ بِهَاۖ وَإِن تُصِبۡهُمۡ سَيِّئَةُۢ بِمَا قَدَّمَتۡ أَيۡدِيهِمۡ فَإِنَّ ٱلۡإِنسَٰنَ كَفُورٞ ٤٨\nThis alludes to the fact that the aim of giving mercy is not to rejoice in pride and insolence, rather, it is to offer thanks to the Bestower. Moreover, the aim of affliction is not for ungratefulness and discontent, rather, it is for returning to the One Who causes it. Al-Alusi: 25/75.\nWhat should the Muslim do during times of prosperity and hardship?\nوَإِن تُصِبۡهُمۡ سَيِّئَةُۢ بِمَا قَدَّمَتۡ أَيۡدِيهِمۡ فَإِنَّ ٱلۡإِنسَٰنَ كَفُورٞ ٤٨\nMeaning: He forgets the previous times of ease and blessings and acknowledges nothing but the present moment. Ibn Kathir: 4/122-123.\nWhat is the difference between how a Muslim and a disbeliever view previous blessings?\nلِّلَّهِ مُلۡكُ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِۚ يَخۡلُقُ مَا يَشَآءُۚ يَهَبُ لِمَن يَشَآءُ إِنَٰثٗا وَيَهَبُ لِمَن يَشَآءُ ٱلذُّكُورَ ٤٩\nIt is said that females are mentioned first to emphasize caring for them due to their weakness, especially when they have recently emerged from pre-Islamic era when female newborns were buried alive. In a Prophetic Hadith: \"Whoever is tested by having daughters and he treats them generously (with benevolence), then they will be a shield for him from the Fire.\" Al-Alusi: 25/75-76.\nIslam honors and protects women. Explain in light of this verse.\nwords\nيَنظُرُونَ مِن طَرفٍ خَفِيٍّLooking with a stealthy glance\nلا مَرَدَّ لَهُIt cannot be averted\nنَكِيرٍYou will not be able to deny your sins\nعَقِيمًاBarren, childless\nمِن وَرَاءِ حِجَابٍFrom behind a veil, like He spoke to Moses (u)"],[489,"§Ash-Shura, Az-Zukhruf\ndeeds\nRecord three useful lessons for worldly matters and three others for religious matters, with which you have been inspired while reflecting on the Quran.\nImagine that the Quran had not reached you and you had not been guided to Islam, how miserable your life would be, then thank Allah for the blessing of guidance and faith.\nWrite an article, or give a talk to your brethren about the virtue and greatness of the Prophets.\nguid\nFollowing the Sunnah of the Prophet (ﷺ) is a reason for attaining guidance.\nThe outcomes of all matters are with Allah, so, do not rely on anyone but Him.\nWhen a heedless person is guided to Islam, he may be more beneficial to Muslims than others.\nrefl\nوَكَذَٰلِكَ أَوۡحَيۡنَآ إِلَيۡكَ رُوحٗا مِّنۡ أَمۡرِنَاۚ\nIt is the Quran; it is called an inspiration because it has a spirit that revives people from the death of ignorance. Malik bin Dinar used to say: O people of the Quran, what did the Quran grow in your hearts?! As the Quran is the spring of the hearts just like the rain is the spring of the earth. Al-Qurtubi: 18/509.\nCalling the Quran an inspiration indicates a deeper meaning. Explain.\nمَا كُنتَ تَدۡرِي مَا ٱلۡكِتَٰبُ وَلَا ٱلۡإِيمَٰنُ\nAllah describes His Messenger (ﷺ) before the revelation, saying: (You did not know what is the Book), which means the essence of it, for he (ﷺ) was illiterate who could not read nor write out of a document; and that highlighted the miracle of the Quran, and made a strong proof of truthfulness of his Prophethood. Al-Shawkani: 4/545.\nThis verse indicates the truthfulness of the Prophet (ﷺ)?\nوَلَٰكِن جَعَلۡنَٰهُ نُورٗا نَّهۡدِي بِهِۦ مَن نَّشَآءُ مِنۡ عِبَادِنَاۚ وَإِنَّكَ لَتَهۡدِيٓ إِلَىٰ صِرَٰطٖ مُّسۡتَقِيمٖ ٥٢\nAllah likens the Book to the light in guidance, as faith, guidance and knowledge resemble the light, while misguidance, ignorance, and disbelief resemble darkness. Allah says, (He brings them out from darknesses into the light) [2:257]. If someone walks on a dark road, he will lose his way, but if there is a light, then he will find his way. So, the light is a means for guidance when no obstacle exists to prevent one from being guided, or else, the light will be of no benefit, as Allah says, (by which We guide whom We will of Our servants). Ibn Ashur: 25/154.\nAllah likens the Book to the light, Why? Who can benefit from the light of the Noble Book?\nوَإِنَّهُۥ فِيٓ أُمِّ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ لَدَيۡنَا لَعَلِيٌّ حَكِيمٌ ٤\nThis explains the high status of the Quran among the highest assembly (the angels), so that the people of the earth respect, venerate, and obey it. Ibn Kathir: 4/124.\nAllah explains the high status of the Quran among the highest assembly. Why?\nأَفَنَضۡرِبُ عَنكُمُ ٱلذِّكۡرَ صَفۡحًا أَن كُنتُمۡ قَوۡمٗا مُّسۡرِفِينَ ٥\nQatadah said: By Allah, had this Quran been lifted when it was first rejected by the former people of this Ummah, they all would have perished, but Allah, by His mercy, repeated it to them again and again. Al-Qurtubi: 19/7.\nHad this Quran been lifted when it was first rejected by the people, what would have happened to us?\nأَفَنَضۡرِبُ عَنكُمُ ٱلذِّكۡرَ صَفۡحًا أَن كُنتُمۡ قَوۡمٗا مُّسۡرِفِينَ ٥\nMeaning: Even if the state in which you are entails leaving and abandoning you so you may die as disbelievers and remain in eternal punishment, but because of Our vast mercy, We will not do that, rather, We will show you the truth through sending the trusted Messenger and revealing the clear Book. Al-Alusi: 25/90.\nHow does this verse show the vast mercy and bounty of Allah?\nوَمَا يَأۡتِيهِم مِّن نَّبِيٍّ إِلَّا كَانُواْ بِهِۦ يَسۡتَهۡزِءُونَ ٧\nThis is a consolation to His Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ). Al-Qurtubi: 19/9.\nWhat is the aim for mentioning the ridicule of previous Prophets by their people?\nwords\nرُوحًاThe Quran, an inspiration to revive the hearts\nصِرَاطٍ مُستَقِيمٍStraight path, Islam\nتَصِيرُAll matters return to Him\nأُمِّ الكِتَابِThe Preserved Tablet\nأَفَنَضرِبُ عَنكُمُ الذِّكرَ صَفحًاShould We then turn the Reminder [Quran] way from you"],[490,"§Az-Zukhruf\ndeeds\nList some of Allah's blessings upon you, by saying: My Lord blessed me with so and so, then, thank Him for them.\nWhen you board a car, an airplane, a ship, an elevator, or an animal, say:\nFind an act of worship done by one of your parents and do it, then supplicate Allah for your parents. Find a misdeed done by one of your parents and avoid it, then supplicate Allah for guidance for your parents.\nguid\nPart of revering Allah is offering worship only to Him.\nThe angels have a great status with Allah.\nOne of the most common things that turn people from the way of Allah is the blind imitation of fathers, and following customs and traditions that are contrary to the Quran and Sunnah.\nrefl\nوَٱلَّذِي نَزَّلَ مِنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ مَآءَۢ بِقَدَرٖ فَأَنشَرۡنَا بِهِۦ بَلۡدَةٗ مَّيۡتٗاۚ\nIbn Abbas said: It means that He sends the rain in due measure, not a drowning deluge like He did to Noah's people nor short of necessary need, so that it will be a livelihood for you and your livestock. Al-Qurtubi: 19/11.\nWhat is the secret behind saying, (in measured amounts)?\nوَٱلَّذِي نَزَّلَ مِنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ مَآءَۢ بِقَدَرٖ فَأَنشَرۡنَا بِهِۦ بَلۡدَةٗ مَّيۡتٗاۚ كَذَٰلِكَ تُخۡرَجُونَ ١١\nAllah shifts from drawing inference and mentioning His blessing in the creation of the earth to drawing inference and mentioning His blessing in the creation of the means of livelihood in it, which is the rainwater that causes plantations on earth to grow as a provision for people. Ibn Ashur: 25/170.\nThe Quran presents proof gradually. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَجَعَلَ لَكُم مِّنَ ٱلۡفُلۡكِ وَٱلۡأَنۡعَٰمِ مَا تَرۡكَبُونَ ١٢ لِتَسۡتَوُۥاْ عَلَىٰ ظُهُورِهِۦ ثُمَّ تَذۡكُرُواْ نِعۡمَةَ رَبِّكُمۡ إِذَا ٱسۡتَوَيۡتُمۡ عَلَيۡهِ وَتَقُولُواْ سُبۡحَٰنَ ٱلَّذِي سَخَّرَ لَنَا هَٰذَا وَمَا كُنَّا لَهُۥ مُقۡرِنِينَ ١٣ وَإِنَّآ إِلَىٰ رَبِّنَا لَمُنقَلِبُونَ ١٤\n(And to our Lord that we will surely return), we will return to Him after our death, and our ultimate destination is with Him. In this verse, the mention of earthly journeys draws attention to the journey of the Hereafter, just as elsewhere, mention of earthly provision draws attention to the importance of ensuring provision for the Hereafter, as Allah says: ( And take provisions for the journey, but the best provision is righteousness) [2:197]. And the mention of earthly raiment is also used to draw attention to the raiment of the Hereafter: (And as adornment. But the raiment of righteousness - that is best) [7:26]. Ibn Kathir: 4/126.\nOur worldly matters often remind us of things related to the Hereafter. Explain in light of previous verses.\nوَإِنَّآ إِلَىٰ رَبِّنَا لَمُنقَلِبُونَ ١٤\nMeaning: Returning back to Allah. This indicates that the rider should reflect on his movement and remember his ultimate return to Allah, thus, bases everything he does during his movement on that thought, and never contradicts it, hence, he rides for a lawful purpose. Moreover, it indicates that riding is not risk-free, therefore, he should remind himself about the Hereafter. Al-Alusi: 25/96.\nRiding animals, and akin to it for travel reminds the rider about the Hereafter. How?\nلِتَسۡتَوُۥاْ عَلَىٰ ظُهُورِهِۦ ثُمَّ تَذۡكُرُواْ نِعۡمَةَ رَبِّكُمۡ إِذَا ٱسۡتَوَيۡتُمۡ عَلَيۡهِ وَتَقُولُواْ سُبۡحَٰنَ ٱلَّذِي سَخَّرَ لَنَا هَٰذَا وَمَا كُنَّا لَهُۥ مُقۡرِنِينَ ١٣ وَإِنَّآ إِلَىٰ رَبِّنَا لَمُنقَلِبُونَ ١٤\nMuslim narrated that when the Prophet (ﷺ) sat on his camel, he said \"God is most great\" three times, then he said, \"Glory be to Him Who has subjected this for us, for we could not have done it by ourselves, and to our Lord that we will surely return.\" Then, he said, \"O Allah, I ask You in this journey of mine from the righteousness and piety and actions that please You. O Allah, ease for us the path, and make near for us the distance of the land. O Allah, You are the companion in the journey, and the caretaker for the family. O Allah, accompany us in our journey, and take care of our families.\" And when he would return to his family, he would say: \"[We are] Returning, if Allah wills, repenting, worshiping, and to our Lord directing the praise.\" Al-Biqai: 7/13.\nHow can someone practice this verse?\nأَمِ ٱتَّخَذَ مِمَّا يَخۡلُقُ بَنَاتٖ وَجَعَلُواْ ٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةَ ٱلَّذِينَ هُمۡ عِبَٰدُ ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنِ إِنَٰثًاۚ\nThey showed disrespect to the angels who are close to Allah, and raised them from the status of humble servants to the status of partners to Allah in some of His unique attributes, then they brought them down from the status of male to female. Glory be to the One Who highlights the contradictions of those who tell lies against Him and oppose His Messengers. Al-Saadi: 764.\nThe polytheists clearly contradict themselves. Explain.\nأَوَ مَن يُنَشَّؤُاْ فِي ٱلۡحِلۡيَةِ وَهُوَ فِي ٱلۡخِصَامِ غَيۡرُ مُبِينٖ ١٨\nBeing brought up in ornaments and soft life is considered infirmity, which is associated with women. Man should avoid that and resent it, as Omar (t) said: \"Wear simple clothes, eat simple food, and emulate the way of life of Ma'd, [an Arab tribe that was known for its tough way of life]; and if some of you want to beautify himself, let him beautify his inside with piety.\" Al-Alusi: 25/99.\nDo ornament and soft living befit the man? Why?\nwords\nبِقَدَرٍA measured amount\nمُقرِنِينَWe could not have done it\nوَأَصفَاكُمHe favored you\nكَظِيمٌFilled with grief\nيُنَشَّأُBrought up\nالحِليَةِOrnaments"],[491,"§Az-Zukhruf\ndeeds\nMake a plan to rid of all types of luxury in your life that induce you to commit a sin or neglect a duty.\nWrite down three manifestations of the Oneness of Allah that Abraham (u) has attained.\nRecord what you have witnessed today of the types of Allah's subjection of people in serving one another.\nguid\nA luxurious way of life is among the reasons for arrogance and rejection of the truth, so, beware of that.\nKnow that anyone who preaches to Allah will be subjected to mocking and ridicule, therefore, do not let that distress you, for it is a recurring way.\nPart of Allah's mercy is subjecting some of His servants to serve others. He made the poor in need for the rich and made the rich in need for the poor.\nrefl\nوَإِذۡ قَالَ إِبۡرَٰهِيمُ لِأَبِيهِ وَقَوۡمِهِۦٓ إِنَّنِي بَرَآءٞ مِّمَّا تَعۡبُدُونَ ٢٦\nHaving mentioned the proof to them, [polytheists of Makkah], and warned them of punishment, but it was evident that they were imitators, He reminded them of their greatest father (Abraham), the source of their pride and the one who is more worthy to be followed, for he was the greatest of their fathers and the only one with the proof [for the Oneness of Allah]. Al-Biqai: 7/21.\nThe story of Abraham (u) is related after mentioning the state of the polytheists who persisted in following their fathers. Why?\nوَإِذۡ قَالَ إِبۡرَٰهِيمُ لِأَبِيهِ وَقَوۡمِهِۦٓ إِنَّنِي بَرَآءٞ مِّمَّا تَعۡبُدُونَ ٢٦\nAbraham's disownment of what his father worshiped was a clear indication of avoiding the worship of idols in an intolerant manner, even if the idols worshiper was the closest relative to the believer such as the father. Ibn Ashur: 25/192.\nAbraham mentioned his father before his people in his disownment. Why?\nوَجَعَلَهَا كَلِمَةَۢ بَاقِيَةٗ فِي عَقِبِهِۦ لَعَلَّهُمۡ يَرۡجِعُونَ ٢٨\n(And he made it), this praiseworthy trait, which is the most important of all and the basis of all those characteristics, namely sincerity in worshiping Allah alone and disowning the worship of everything besides Him. This word remained among his descendants until they began to live a life of affluence and transgression. Al-Saadi: 764.\nLuxurious life and transgression have impacts on the belief of the Oneness of Allah. How?\nوَلَمَّا جَآءَهُمُ ٱلۡحَقُّ قَالُواْ هَٰذَا سِحۡرٞ وَإِنَّا بِهِۦ كَٰفِرُونَ ٣٠\nThis is because of their great stubbornness and opposition, for they could not stop at merely turning away from it or merely rejecting it. They were not content until they impugned and criticized it in the worst manner, regarding it as equivalent to magic, which no one brings but the most evil of people and the worst liars and fabricators. Al-Saadi: 765.\nThis saying, (This is magic) reflects the state in which the polytheists were. What was it?\nوَقَالُواْ لَوۡلَا نُزِّلَ هَٰذَا ٱلۡقُرۡءَانُ عَلَىٰ رَجُلٖ مِّنَ ٱلۡقَرۡيَتَيۡنِ عَظِيمٍ ٣١ أَهُمۡ يَقۡسِمُونَ رَحۡمَتَ رَبِّكَۚ نَحۡنُ قَسَمۡنَا بَيۡنَهُم مَّعِيشَتَهُمۡ فِي ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَاۚ\nAs worldly livelihood and provision are in the Hand of Allah, it is He Who distributes it among His servants, so He gives abundant provision to whomever He wills and restricts it for whomever He wills, in accordance with His wisdom. Therefore, it is more appropriate that His religious blessings, the highest of which is the status of being a Prophet or Messenger, should be in the Hand of Allah, for Allah knows best where to place His message. Thus, it is known that their suggestions were flawed and invalid, and the control of all things, both religious and worldly, is in the Hand of Allah alone. Al-Saadi: 765.\nAllah mentions His distribution of provisions after relating their suggestion this Quran should have been sent down upon a great man from one of the two cities. Why?\nوَرَفَعۡنَا بَعۡضَهُمۡ فَوۡقَ بَعۡضٖ دَرَجَٰتٖ لِّيَتَّخِذَ بَعۡضُهُم بَعۡضٗا سُخۡرِيّٗاۗ وَرَحۡمَتُ رَبِّكَ خَيۡرٞ مِّمَّا يَجۡمَعُونَ ٣٢\nThis subjection is for service, which means that We have raised some of them above others in ranks, so that they may serve one another. Ibn Juzay: 2/312.\nThere is great wisdom behind the differences in people’s ranks. What is it?\nوَلَوۡلَآ أَن يَكُونَ ٱلنَّاسُ أُمَّةٗ وَٰحِدَةٗ لَّجَعَلۡنَا لِمَن يَكۡفُرُ بِٱلرَّحۡمَٰنِ لِبُيُوتِهِمۡ سُقُفٗا مِّن فِضَّةٖ وَمَعَارِجَ عَلَيۡهَا يَظۡهَرُونَ ٣٣\nAlhasan said: It means that if it were not that all people would become disbelievers because of their inclination toward the life of this world and neglecting the Hereafter, We would have given them in this life what has been described. That is because of the insignificance of worldly life to Allah. Al-Qurtubi: 19/37-38.\nIn light of this verse, explain how insignificant this worldly life to Allah.\nwords\nبَرَاءٌI disown\nفَطَرَنِيCreated me\nسُخرِيًّاWorking for each other\nوَمَعَارِجَSilver stairways\nيَظهَرُونَThey ascend"],[492,"§Az-Zukhruf\ndeeds\nSay, \"Glorified is Allah and praised is He, Glorified is Allah the Great.\" as many as a hundred times.\nBecome familiar with an abandoned Sunnah, and try to practice and hold fast to it.\nRecall long times that had passed in which you did not remember Allah, then remember that the devil was your companion throughout these time periods.\nguid\nBeware of acting upon something thinking that you are rightly guided while, in fact, you are not. The remedy for that is becoming knowledgeable of the authentic proof.\nAdhering to the Book [the Quran] and Sunnah is a protection and salvation in worldly life and the Hereafter.\nRidiculing the religion and the believers is among the traits of the disbelievers and hypocrites.\nrefl\nلَّجَعَلۡنَا لِمَن يَكۡفُرُ بِٱلرَّحۡمَٰنِ لِبُيُوتِهِمۡ سُقُفٗا مِّن فِضَّةٖ وَمَعَارِجَ عَلَيۡهَا يَظۡهَرُونَ ٣٣ وَلِبُيُوتِهِمۡ أَبۡوَٰبٗا وَسُرُرًا عَلَيۡهَا يَتَّكِـُٔونَ ٣٤ وَزُخۡرُفٗاۚ وَإِن كُلُّ ذَٰلِكَ لَمَّا مَتَٰعُ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَاۚ\nMeaning: He would have made their lives full of luxurious things, and given them everything they desire. But what prevented Him from doing that was His mercy towards His servants, lest they hasten to disbelieve and commit many sins because of their love of worldly gain. This indicates that He may withhold some worldly gains from His servants, at society's level, or individuals, in their best interests. Al-Saadi: 765.\nThis verse contains proof that Allah, out of His mercy, may withhold some of life's ornaments from His servants. Explain.\nوَمَن يَعۡشُ عَن ذِكۡرِ ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنِ نُقَيِّضۡ لَهُۥ شَيۡطَٰنٗا فَهُوَ لَهُۥ قَرِينٞ ٣٦ وَإِنَّهُمۡ لَيَصُدُّونَهُمۡ عَنِ ٱلسَّبِيلِ وَيَحۡسَبُونَ أَنَّهُم مُّهۡتَدُونَ ٣٧\nA person who lives in prosperity is likely to be distracted from remembering Allah, so, the angels would repel from him, but the devils would cling to him, which would lead him to every evil deed. But whoever fears Allah and adheres to His remembrance, Allah will assign to him a helping angel. Al-Biqai: 7/27-28.\nMention some of the negative consequences of being heedless of Allah’s remembrance.\nوَإِنَّهُمۡ لَيَصُدُّونَهُمۡ عَنِ ٱلسَّبِيلِ وَيَحۡسَبُونَ أَنَّهُم مُّهۡتَدُونَ ٣٧\nIf it is asked: Does this person have any excuse because he thinks that he is rightly guided while he is not? The response is: No, he and his ilk have no excuse, because the cause of their ignorance is turning away from the reminder of Allah, despite of their ability to choose guidance. They showed no interest in guidance despite being able to do so, but they chose falsehood. So, the fault is theirs and the error is theirs. Al-Saadi: 766.\nDo the misguided people have any excuse because they thought that they were rightly guided while they were not?\nوَلَن يَنفَعَكُمُ ٱلۡيَوۡمَ إِذ ظَّلَمۡتُمۡ أَنَّكُمۡ فِي ٱلۡعَذَابِ مُشۡتَرِكُونَ ٣٩\nThis is said to the disbelievers in the Hereafter, which means that they will not be consoled by sharing the punishment, similar to the relief that an afflicted person, in worldly life, would feel when seeing others with the same affliction. Ibn Juzay: 2/314.\nExplain the mental punishment to which a heedless person will be subjected, in the Hereafter.\nأَفَأَنتَ تُسۡمِعُ ٱلصُّمَّ أَوۡ تَهۡدِي ٱلۡعُمۡيَ وَمَن كَانَ فِي ضَلَٰلٖ مُّبِينٖ ٤٠\nMeaning: None of that is up to you, rather, it is all in the Hand of Allah, the Most Powerful over all things. As to you [O Prophet], your duty is only to convey the message. Al-Biqai: 7/30.\nWhat is the main task of those who preach others to Allah?\nوَإِنَّهُۥ لَذِكۡرٞ لَّكَ وَلِقَوۡمِكَۖ وَسَوۡفَ تُسۡـَٔلُونَ ٤٤\nThe pronoun in (it is) refers to the Quran or Islam. (Remembrance) means honor. (Your people), Quraish and the rest of the Arab people, as they, through Islam, have attained honor in worldly life and the Hereafter. It should suffice you that they had conquered the east and west of the land. Ibn Juzay: 2/314.\nWhat is the honor attained by the Arabs when they adhered to Islam?\nوَلَقَدۡ أَرۡسَلۡنَا مُوسَىٰ بِـَٔايَٰتِنَآ إِلَىٰ فِرۡعَوۡنَ وَمَلَإِيْهِۦ فَقَالَ إِنِّي رَسُولُ رَبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٤٦\nThose who live in luxury often disdain whoever comes to them, and they persist on doing that until the Almighty subjugates them by the Message carried out by His Messengers, either by destroying them or something else despite their power. Allah relates the story of Moses (u) as a testimony to this fact, such as the answer of Pharaoh to Moses (u), his subsequent demise despite his power, and the deliverance of the Children of Israel despite their weakness. Al-Biqai: 7/33.\nWhat is the attitude of the affluent ones toward those who advise them? What is Allah’s way in deciding the end of each group?\nwords\nوَزُخرُفًاGold\nوَإِن كُلُّ ذَلِكَ لَمَّاAll of these are mere\nيَعشُTurns away\nنُقَيِّضWe assign\nقَرِينٌA companion\nبُعدَ المَشرِقَينِThe distance between the east and west"],[493,"§Az-Zukhruf\ndeeds\nRecall a calamity that befell you, then recall a sin that you had committed before it, and ask for Allah's forgiveness. Perhaps the calamity was a reminder to turn to Allah.\nReflect on the sequence of calamities upon the Ummah, minor and major ones, then say, \"O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your wrath, and I seek refuge in Your forgiveness from Your punishment.\"\nGive to charity, for it extinguishes the wrath of Allah.\nguid\nThe calamities that befall people are a warning from Allah for them to repent and return to Him.\nKeep away from sins and disobeying the command of His Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ) in order to be saved from Allah’s wrath and punishment.\nBeware of transgressions in words and deeds, for it leads to humiliation in this world and the Hereafter. When Pharoah's people transgressed, Allah sent His punishment upon them.\nrefl\nوَمَا نُرِيهِم مِّنۡ ءَايَةٍ إِلَّا هِيَ أَكۡبَرُ مِنۡ أُخۡتِهَاۖ وَأَخَذۡنَٰهُم بِٱلۡعَذَابِ لَعَلَّهُمۡ يَرۡجِعُونَ ٤٨\nAllah reveals that the reason for seizing them with punishment was so that they may turn in repentance. Al-Shawkani: 4/559.\nAllah's mercy toward His servants manifests in His worldly punishment. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَقَالُواْ يَٰٓأَيُّهَ ٱلسَّاحِرُ ٱدۡعُ لَنَا رَبَّكَ بِمَا عَهِدَ عِندَكَ إِنَّنَا لَمُهۡتَدُونَ ٤٩\n(O magician) meaning Moses (u). This was either by way of ridiculing him, or because for them addressing someone in this manner was a kind of praise, so they beseeched him by addressing him as they addressed their so-called scholars, namely the magicians. Al-Saadi: 767.\nScholars and worshipers are indispensable to the society. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَنَادَىٰ فِرۡعَوۡنُ فِي قَوۡمِهِۦ قَالَ يَٰقَوۡمِ أَلَيۡسَ لِي مُلۡكُ مِصۡرَ وَهَٰذِهِ ٱلۡأَنۡهَٰرُ تَجۡرِي مِن تَحۡتِيٓۚ أَفَلَا تُبۡصِرُونَ ٥١\nThis stemmed from his enormous ignorance, for he took pride in something that was not connected to his attitude and character, and he did not take pride in praiseworthy characteristics or righteous deeds. Al-Saadi: 767.\nPharaoh's praise of himself reflects his enormous ignorance. Explain.\nفَلَوۡلَآ أُلۡقِيَ عَلَيۡهِ أَسۡوِرَةٞ مِّن ذَهَبٍ أَوۡ جَآءَ مَعَهُ ٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ مُقۡتَرِنِينَ ٥٣\nHe looked only at outward appearances and did not understand the true inner matters that are clearer than what he focused on, if only he had understood that. Ibn Kathir: 4/132.\nPharaoh had an invalid assessment of Moses. Explain.\nفَٱسۡتَخَفَّ قَوۡمَهُۥ فَأَطَاعُوهُۚ إِنَّهُمۡ كَانُواْ قَوۡمٗا فَٰسِقِينَ ٥٤\nMeaning: He befooled his people, the Copts; he found them ignorant. It is said that he incited recklessness and ignorance among them. Al-Baghawi: 4/103.\nIgnorance is among the reasons for the spread of religious innovation and misguidance. Explain.\nفَلَمَّآ ءَاسَفُونَا ٱنتَقَمۡنَا مِنۡهُمۡ فَأَغۡرَقۡنَٰهُمۡ أَجۡمَعِينَ ٥٥\nOmar bin Tharr said: \"O disobedient people, do not be deluded by Allah’s long forbearance toward you and beware of His anger, because He said, (and when they angered Us, We took retribution from them).\"Al-Qurtubi: 19/64..\nIn light of this verse, explain the risk of excessive disobedience and delusion.\nفَجَعَلۡنَٰهُمۡ سَلَفٗا وَمَثَلٗا لِّلۡأٓخِرِينَ ٥٦\nTheir plight became an admonishment for some and misguiding for others. Whoever decides to emulate them and have the same fate, will do as they did; and whoever wants to be saved from their fate, will avoid doing what they did. Al-Biqai: 7/39.\nHow does Allah make the plight of former nations an admonishment for some and misguiding for others?\nwords\nيَنكُثُونَThey broke their promise\nمَهِينٌInsignificant\nمُقتَرِنِينَIn conjunction to support him\nآسَفُونَاThey angered Us"],[494,"§Az-Zukhruf\ndeeds\nCollaborate with a friend of yours to be in the first row for the prayer and to recite the Quran.\nPay a visit to one of your Muslim brethren for no purpose except for sensing the love for the sake of Allah.\nSay, \"Our Lord, let our spouses and children be a source of joy for us, and make us good examples for the righteous.\"\nguid\nBeware of division in religion.\nFollow the path of Allah in all matters, and do not deviate from it.\nFriendships that are based on worldly benefits will turn into enmities on the Day of Resurrection.\nrefl\nوَإِنَّهُۥ لَعِلۡمٞ لِّلسَّاعَةِ فَلَا تَمۡتَرُنَّ بِهَا وَٱتَّبِعُونِۚ هَٰذَا صِرَٰطٞ مُّسۡتَقِيمٞ ٦١\n(A sign of the Hour), based on the true and authentic view that is attested by the Holy Quran and the Sunnah of the Prophet (ﷺ), the coming of Jesus (u) near the end of time to earth will be a sign that the beginning of the Hour is near, for the return of Jesus (u) alive near the end of time is one of the major signs of the Hour. Al-Shanqiti: 7/128.\nWhat is meant by: (A sign of the Hour)?\nوَلَا يَصُدَّنَّكُمُ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُۖ إِنَّهُۥ لَكُمۡ عَدُوّٞ مُّبِينٞ ٦٢\nMeaning: Satan's enmity toward you is evident and proclaimed by him against your father until he caused him -and eventually yourselves- to be expelled from the place of comfort to the place of hardship. His enmity is based on envy, which makes it eternal. Al-Biqai: 7/43.\nWhat is the basis for satan’s enmity toward us? When will it end?\nإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ هُوَ رَبِّي وَرَبُّكُمۡ فَٱعۡبُدُوهُۚ هَٰذَا صِرَٰطٞ مُّسۡتَقِيمٞ ٦٤\nJesus (u) began with himself before his people when saying, (Allah is my Lord and your Lord) in order to block all means to glorify Him. This speech, in fact, was one of his miracles because Allah knows that some of his followers would go to extremes and claim that he was a son of Allah. Ibn Ashur: 25/248.\nJesus (u) began with himself before his people when saying, (Allah is my Lord and your Lord). Why?\nٱلۡأَخِلَّآءُ يَوۡمَئِذِۢ بَعۡضُهُمۡ لِبَعۡضٍ عَدُوٌّ إِلَّا ٱلۡمُتَّقِينَ ٦٧\nMeaning: Every friendship that exists for a purpose other than the sake of Allah will turn to enmity on the Day of Resurrection, except for that which is for the sake of Allah, which will last forever. Ibn Kathir: 4/135.\nWhat will ensure the continuation of friendship on the Day of Resurrection?\nيَٰعِبَادِ لَا خَوۡفٌ عَلَيۡكُمُ ٱلۡيَوۡمَ وَلَآ أَنتُمۡ تَحۡزَنُونَ ٦٨\nMeaning: You will have no fear with regard to what you expect to happen in the future, and you will feel no grief for what happened in the past. Once it is established that there is no fear or distress with regard to the future or the past, then what one loves and seeks is certain. Al-Saadi: 769.\nWhen people of Paradise do not have fear nor grief, then what becomes certain for them?\nيُطَافُ عَلَيۡهِم بِصِحَافٖ مِّن ذَهَبٖ وَأَكۡوَابٖۖ وَفِيهَا مَا تَشۡتَهِيهِ ٱلۡأَنفُسُ وَتَلَذُّ ٱلۡأَعۡيُنُۖ وَأَنتُمۡ فِيهَا خَٰلِدُونَ ٧١ وَتِلۡكَ ٱلۡجَنَّةُ ٱلَّتِيٓ أُورِثۡتُمُوهَا بِمَا كُنتُمۡ تَعۡمَلُونَ ٧٢ لَكُمۡ فِيهَا فَٰكِهَةٞ كَثِيرَةٞ\nWhen food and drink are mentioned, fruit is also mentioned to complete the picture of blessing and joy. Ibn Kathir: 4/137.\nThe fruit is mentioned right after mentioning food and drink. Why?\nوَتِلۡكَ ٱلۡجَنَّةُ ٱلَّتِيٓ أُورِثۡتُمُوهَا بِمَا كُنتُمۡ تَعۡمَلُونَ ٧٢\nThis will be said to them on the Day of Resurrection, which means that Paradise is yours, just as an inheritor takes his inheritance, for the righteous deeds you used to do in worldly life. Al-Shawkani: 4/564.\nGiven this verse, how important is a righteous deed?\nwords\nلَعِلمٌ لِلسَّاعَةِThe coming of Jesus (u) indicates that the beginning of the Hour is near\nصِرَاطٌ مُستَقِيمٌA straight path to Paradise\nبِالحِكمَةِProphethood\nبَغتَةًSuddenly\nالأَخِلاَّءُClose friends\nتُحبَرُونَRejoicing in bliss\nبِصِحَافٍPlates, trays"],[495,"§Az-Zukhruf\ndeeds\nAct upon this verse by glorifying Allah.\nSupplicate Allah to grant you the intercession of the Prophet (ﷺ).\nPardon someone who wronged you today.\nguid\nThe encompassment and vastness of Allah's knowledge drives His servant to fear and observe His limits.\nExalting Allah above the fabrications of disbelievers in ascribing a son to Him.\nAllah enjoins His Prophet to pardon the disbelievers, so, should not we pardon those who wronged us?\nrefl\nلَا يُفَتَّرُ عَنۡهُمۡ وَهُمۡ فِيهِ مُبۡلِسُونَ ٧٥\nThey will despair of being saved, hence, they succumb to the torment and punishment. Al-Tabari: 21/643.\nWhat is meant by: (They, therein, are in despair)?\nلَا يُفَتَّرُ عَنۡهُمۡ وَهُمۡ فِيهِ مُبۡلِسُونَ ٧٥\nMeaning: They will grieve due to the despair. In the Arabic text, the word used for (they, therein, are in despair) is \"Mublisoon.\" Al-Raghib said: Iblas is the grief due to extreme despair, and the name \"Iblees\" is derived from it. The \"Mublis\" often remains quiet and forgets what concerns him, hence, when someone becomes quiet and has nothing to say, he is described as \"Ablasa.\" Therefore, here \"Iblas\" is interpreted as silence and the loss of argument. Al-Alusi: 25/141.\nWhat is the meaning of \"Mublisoon\"?\nقَالَ إِنَّكُم مَّٰكِثُونَ ٧٧ لَقَدۡ جِئۡنَٰكُم بِٱلۡحَقِّ وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكۡثَرَكُمۡ لِلۡحَقِّ كَٰرِهُونَ ٧٨\nWhen they ask to be allowed to die, Malik will answer them: (Indeed, you will remain), which means that you will have no way out from it and no refuge. Then, the reason why they are doomed will be given, which is their stubborn resistance to the truth. Allah says: (We surely brought you the truth, but most of you were averse to the truth). Ibn Kathir: 4/137.\nThe verse (We surely brought you the truth) comes after (Indeed, you will remain). Why?\nلَقَدۡ جِئۡنَٰكُم بِٱلۡحَقِّ وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكۡثَرَكُمۡ لِلۡحَقِّ كَٰرِهُونَ ٧٨\nMeaning: In worldly life, We have brought you the truth, which is the Oneness of Allah, and the requirements of faith by sending the Messengers and revealing the Scriptures, but most of you were averse to the truth, any truth, repelled from it and rejecting it. Al-Alusi: 25/142.\nWhat is meant by (the truth) in this verse?\nقُلۡ إِن كَانَ لِلرَّحۡمَٰنِ وَلَدٞ فَأَنَا۠ أَوَّلُ ٱلۡعَٰبِدِينَ ٨١\n(Then I would be the first of [his] worshipers) namely that son, because he would be a part of his father, and I am the first of humankind to submit to that which is beloved to Allah. But I am the first to reject this notion and the most emphatic in denying it. Thus, it is known that it is false. This is a strong argument, for those who know how the Messengers really are. Al-Saadi: 770.\nThis verse indicates that the Messengers have always pursued perfection and kept away from evil. Explain this useful lesson.\nسُبۡحَٰنَ رَبِّ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ رَبِّ ٱلۡعَرۡشِ عَمَّا يَصِفُونَ ٨٢\nAllah mentions the heavens and earth to indicate that He encompasses the worlds of arrangement and creation, since the polytheists associated partners to Him on earth, which were their idols, and attributed daughters to Him in heavens, which were the angels. Ibn Ashur: 25/267.\nAllah mentions that He is the Lord of the heavens and earth. Why?\nفَٱصۡفَحۡ عَنۡهُمۡ وَقُلۡ سَلَٰمٞۚ فَسَوۡفَ يَعۡلَمُونَ ٨٩\nHe was not enjoined to greet them, rather, he was enjoined to leave them, which means if you reject my Message, then I will leave you in peace. Al-Alusi: 25/151.\nWe are enjoined to be lenient and wise against the rejection of those whom we preach. Explain in light of this verse.\nwords\nلاَ يُفَتَّرُ عَنهُمIt will not be lightened for them\nمُبلِسُونَThey will despair of Allah’s mercy\nأَم أَبرَمُوا أَمرًاHave they devised a plan against the Prophet\nيَخُوضُواThey converse vainly\nفَأَنَّى يُؤفَكُونَHow then are they turned away from the worship of Allah\nوَقِيلِهِMuhammad's saying in his complaint about his people\nفَاصفَحTurn aside from them"],[496,"§Ad-Dukhan\ndeeds\nWhen you wake up in the morning, say, \"All praise be to Allah who gave me life after having taken it from me, and to Him is the resurrection.\"\nSupplicate Allah to remove affliction from the afflicted ones.\nRevere the Prophet (ﷺ) by asking Allah to confer blessing upon him and grant him peace.\nguid\nAmong the virtues of the night of the Decree are: Revelation of the Quran, and distribution of provisions, so, ensure to benefit from it by praying, reciting the Quran and remembering Allah throughout the night.\nWhen reminded of Allah, take heed and do not be of those who are arrogant, lest Allah blocks your insight.\nAllah gives respite but never neglects.\nrefl\nإِنَّآ أَنزَلۡنَٰهُ فِي لَيۡلَةٖ مُّبَٰرَكَةٍۚ إِنَّا كُنَّا مُنذِرِينَ ٣\n(During a blessed night), one in which there was much good and blessing, namely the night of the Decree (Laylat Al-Qadr), which is better than a thousand months. Thus, He sent down the best of words on the best of nights and days, to the best of people, in the language of the Arabs. Al-Saadi: 773.\nWhat is meant by the blessed night? Why is it described as: A blessed?\nفِيهَا يُفۡرَقُ كُلُّ أَمۡرٍ حَكِيمٍ ٤\n(Is determined), decreed. (Matter of wisdom) is the servants’ provisions, their destinies, and all of their matters for that particular year. It is copied off the Preserved Tablet so that the angels can follow its manifestation throughout the coming year. Ibn Juzay: 2/321.\nWhat is the matter of wisdom that is determined on the night of the Decree?\nبَلۡ هُمۡ فِي شَكّٖ يَلۡعَبُونَ ٩\nTheir acknowledgment of the Lordship of Allah was not based on knowledge and certain conviction. Rather, it was as good as nonexistent, because they mixed it with doubt and frivolity, hence, it lacked certainty and admission, which is putting the knowledge into practice. If one does not practice what he knows and maintain it, it will be forgotten until it turns into doubts. Ibn Ashur: 25/284-285.\nGiven this verse, explain the risk of not practicing what you know.\nفَٱرۡتَقِبۡ يَوۡمَ تَأۡتِي ٱلسَّمَآءُ بِدُخَانٖ مُّبِينٖ ١٠\nAbu Huraira (t) narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"Hasten to do good deeds before six things occur: The Antichrist, the Smoke, Beast of the Earth, the rising of the sun from the west, that which will happen to all people (Day of Resurrection), and that which will happen to each of you (death).\" Al-Biqai: 7/68.\nWhat are the negative consequences of procrastinating good deeds?\nرَّبَّنَا ٱكۡشِفۡ عَنَّا ٱلۡعَذَابَ إِنَّا مُؤۡمِنُونَ ١٢\n(We are believers) is a justification for their request to remove the torment from them, which means that we have become immune to the punishment that is deserved by the disbelievers. Their statement points to the high honor of faith. Ibn Ashur: 25/290.\nThis verse points to the high honor of faith. How?\n۞وَلَقَدۡ فَتَنَّا قَبۡلَهُمۡ قَوۡمَ فِرۡعَوۡنَ وَجَآءَهُمۡ رَسُولٞ كَرِيمٌ ١٧\n(A noble messenger), Qatadah said: This refers to Moses (u), and Allah describes him as noble because he has a high status with Him. Moreover, he is described as such since he has a high standing with his people. Al-Tabari: 22/24.\nMoses (u) is described as noble. Why?\nإِنِّي لَكُمۡ رَسُولٌ أَمِينٞ ١٨\nMeaning: A Messenger from the Lord of the worlds, faithful to the purpose for which He has sent me; I do not withhold anything of the message from you, and I do not add anything to it, or take anything away from it, and this requires you to submit completely to Him. Al-Saadi: 773.\nThis verse contains a censure for religious innovation. Explain.\nwords\nلَيلَةٍ مُبَارَكَةٍThe night of the Decree in the month of Ramadan\nيُفرَقُWhat is inscribed in the Preserved Table is transferred to the scribes among the angels\nأَمرٍ حَكِيمٍMatters that are wisely determined each year such as provisions and destinies\nفَارتَقِبWait with these polytheists\nالبَطشَةَ الكُبرَىThe greatest assault on the Day of Resurrection\nأَدُّوا إِلَيَّDeliver to me the servants of Allah"],[497,"§Ad-Dukhan\ndeeds\nSeek refuge with Allah from a frightening enemy, harm, or akin to that.\nThink of a disbeliever who has excessively committed crimes against the believers, and invoke Allah's punishment upon him.\nPray two Rak'as in a place at which you never prayed before so that it will testify for you.\nguid\nThe heaven and earth weep for the believer after his death because of his righteous deeds, so, do righteous deeds to attain that.\nAllah's power to destroy the transgressors is great.\nCaution must be taken from the reasons of the destruction of nations.\nrefl\nوَإِن لَّمۡ تُؤۡمِنُواْ لِي فَٱعۡتَزِلُونِ ٢١ فَدَعَا رَبَّهُۥٓ أَنَّ هَٰٓؤُلَآءِ قَوۡمٞ مُّجۡرِمُونَ ٢٢\nMeaning: Then, let us leave one another alone and live in peace until Allah judges between us. After Moses (u) had stayed among them for a long time, and the proof of Allah had been established against them, but that only increased them in disbelief and stubbornness, he prayed to his Lord against them, a prayer that was answered. Ibn Kathir: 4/143.\nWhat made Moses pray to Allah against them after he had preached them?\nفَمَا بَكَتۡ عَلَيۡهِمُ ٱلسَّمَآءُ وَٱلۡأَرۡضُ\nMeaning: They had no righteous deeds which used to ascend through the gates of the heavens that would weep for them when they died, and they had no places on earth where they used to worship Allah which would notice their loss. Hence, they did not deserve to be given a respite, because of their disbelief, sin, transgression, and stubbornness. Ibn Kathir: 4/144.\nWhat is the reason that makes the heavens and earth weep for the servants?\nفَمَا بَكَتۡ عَلَيۡهِمُ ٱلسَّمَآءُ وَٱلۡأَرۡضُ وَمَا كَانُواْ مُنظَرِينَ ٢٩\nThis is a proclamation of disregard for their demise. The interpreters said: They did not do righteous deeds on earth so that it would weep for them, and no good deed for them had ever ascended through the heavens so that that it would weep for them. This means that none of the inhabitants of the earth and heavens was affected by their demise. Al-Shawkani: 4/575.\nDescribe the insignificance of the polytheists in light of this verse.\nوَلَقَدِ ٱخۡتَرۡنَٰهُمۡ عَلَىٰ عِلۡمٍ عَلَى ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٣٢ وَءَاتَيۡنَٰهُم مِّنَ ٱلۡأٓيَٰتِ مَا فِيهِ بَلَٰٓؤٞاْ مُّبِينٌ ٣٣\nThe tribe of Quraish used to take pride in worldly ornaments and consider them as a sign of Allah’s pleasure with them while considering indigence a fall into misery and a sign of being far from Allah. Therefore, Allah responded to their claim by stating that which He had given to the Children of Israel despite their weakness and miserable life after eradicating Pharaoh and his people. Al-Biqai: 7/76.\nIs prosperity in worldly life a sign of Allah’s pleasure with the rich? Is indigence a sign of Allah's displeasure with the poor?\nأَهُمۡ خَيۡرٌ أَمۡ قَوۡمُ تُبَّعٖ وَٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبۡلِهِمۡ أَهۡلَكۡنَٰهُمۡۚ إِنَّهُمۡ كَانُواْ مُجۡرِمِينَ ٣٧\nAfter presenting them with the example of the destruction of Pharaoh, Allah presents another example that is closer to them, who are the people of Tubba. Arabs used to hear about the grave destruction of Tubba (a king) and his people in Yemen. During their travel, many Arabs had witnessed the ruins of their kingdom, which indicated their great power, and conversed about their demise by the flood of the dam (Arim). Ibn Ashur: 25/308.\nWhat is the use of presenting the example of the people of Tubba?\nأَهُمۡ خَيۡرٌ أَمۡ قَوۡمُ تُبَّعٖ وَٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبۡلِهِمۡ أَهۡلَكۡنَٰهُمۡۚ إِنَّهُمۡ كَانُواْ مُجۡرِمِينَ ٣٧\nMeaning: Is the tribe of Quraish more powerful than the people of Tubba and the disbelievers before them? As We had destroyed the people of Tubba and others when they denied, We are quite capable of destroying these people [Quraish]. This was meant as a threat to them. Ibn Juzay: 2/324.\nClarify the threat in this verse.\nوَمَا خَلَقۡنَا ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضَ وَمَا بَيۡنَهُمَا لَٰعِبِينَ ٣٨ مَا خَلَقۡنَٰهُمَآ إِلَّا بِٱلۡحَقِّ وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكۡثَرَهُمۡ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٣٩\nBecause of their lack of knowledge, they dare to disobey Allah and spread corruption on earth, as they do not hope for reward nor do they fear punishment. Al-Biqai: 7/79.\nWhat dares the servant to pursue sins and corruption? What drives a person to stay on a straight path and righteousness?\nwords\nوَأَن لاَ تَعلُواDo not be arrogant\nبِسُلطَانٍProof\nعُذتُI sought refuge\nأَن تَرجُمُونِLest you stone me to death\nرَهوًاCalm and still\nمُنظَرِينَReprieved from punishment\nاختَرنَاهُمWe chose them\nبِمُنشَرِينَWill be resurrected"],[498,"§Ad-Dukhan\ndeeds\nSupplicate Allah to have mercy upon you on the Day of Judgment.\nSay, \"O Allah, I seek refuge with You from the Fire and those words and deeds that bring me closer to it.\"\nAsk Allah to be among those who will be in a safe place within gardens and springs.\nguid\nOn the Day of Resurrection, the disbelievers will face a great deal of torment, humiliation and rebuke.\nEvery blessing that the believer receive is a benevolence from Allah.\nAmong the objectives of revealing the Quran are reminding and admonishing.\nrefl\nإِلَّا مَن رَّحِمَ ٱللَّهُۚ إِنَّهُۥ هُوَ ٱلۡعَزِيزُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ ٤٢\n(The All-Mighty): None has the ability to change what He decrees, as He is Merciful toward whomever He wills. (The Most Merciful): His mercy is vast toward whomever He wills from among His servants in accordance with His knowledge, wisdom, and promise, as stated in this Hadith: \"Be merciful toward those who are on earth, and you will be shown mercy from One Who is above the heavens.\" Ibn Ashur: 25/31.\nThis verse ends with these two holy Names (the All-Mighty, the Most Merciful). Why?\nذُقۡ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ ٱلۡعَزِيزُ ٱلۡكَرِيمُ ٤٩\nThis will be said to the disbeliever by way of rebuking and mocking him. It means that you were the honored and noble to yourself. Abu Jahl [a leader of the disbelievers in Makkah] said: In between these two mountains, there is none who is more noble and honored than me. Ibn Juzay: 2/324.\nOn the Day of Resurrection, how will the disbeliever be called (honored) while he is in the Fire?\nإِنَّ ٱلۡمُتَّقِينَ فِي مَقَامٍ أَمِينٖ ٥١\nSafety is the most important feature of a good place, as the inhabitant's priority is seeking safety from fears and undesirable things. When he finds safety in his place, he will be at ease and enjoy his attained bliss. Ibn Ashur: 25/317.\nGiven this verse, explain the great blessing of safety.\nيَلۡبَسُونَ مِن سُندُسٖ وَإِسۡتَبۡرَقٖ مُّتَقَٰبِلِينَ ٥٣\nMeaning: Sitting on thrones where none of them will sit with his back to anyone else. Ibn Kathir: 4/148.\nIn Paradise, there will be no insulting behaviors. Explain in light of this verse.\nيَدۡعُونَ فِيهَا بِكُلِّ فَٰكِهَةٍ ءَامِنِينَ ٥٥\nMeaning: The fruit in Paradise is not like the worldly fruit that we consume, but fear its ill effects and depletion. Al-Tabari: 22/53.\nIn this verse, the fruit in Paradise is mentioned with safety and security. Why?\nفَإِنَّمَا يَسَّرۡنَٰهُ بِلِسَانِكَ لَعَلَّهُمۡ يَتَذَكَّرُونَ ٥٨\nMeaning: We have made this Quran, which We have sent down, easy, plain and clear, in your language which is the most eloquent, clear and beautiful of all languages. Ibn Kathir: 4/149.\nDiscuss the advantage of the Arabic language over other languages in light of this verse.\nفَٱرۡتَقِبۡ إِنَّهُم مُّرۡتَقِبُونَ ٥٩\nMeaning: Wait and watch when We give you victory over them and destroy them, while they wait for the opposite of that. This verse contains a promise and a threat. Ibn Juzay: 2/325.\nExplain how this verse combine a promise with a threat.\nwords\nالأَثِيمِOne who has committed major sins\nكَالمُهلِMurky oil\nفَاعتِلُوهُSeize him and drag him\nسُندُسٍFine silk\nوَإِستَبرَقٍHeavy brocade\nالمَوتَةَ الأُولَىThe first death in worldly life\nفَارتَقِبWait for your victory and their demise"],[499,"§Al-Jathiyah\ndeeds\nReflect on how a man, a camel, and a snake move about, and record the differences between them and what that indicates.\nWrite down three benefits from the alternation of the night and day.\nRecall a sin that you committed, and remember a verse that forbids it, then ask for Allah’s forgiveness.\nguid\nWhen you receive a piece of information from Allah, [through the Quran] and His Messenger (ﷺ) [through his Sunnah], that is sufficient, hence, do not follow the desires of men.\nNever ridicule anything related to the religion, for it is a grave sin.\nReflecting on the creations of Allah is very helpful to the servant to reach gratefulness and Oneness of Allah.\nrefl\nتَنزِيلُ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ مِنَ ٱللَّهِ ٱلۡعَزِيزِ ٱلۡحَكِيمِ ٢\nAmong all of Allah's holy names, these two, (the All-Mighty, the All-Wise) are singled for mention to indicate that what is revealed from (the All-Mighty) suits His Might, hence, it is a mighty Book, as Allah describes it, (and indeed, it is a mighty Book) [41:41], which means it overpowers those who oppose it because they were unable to match it. The holy name (the All-Wise) indicates that what is revealed from Him suits His wisdom. Ibn Ashur: 25/325.\nAmong Allah's holy names, these two, (the All-Mighty, the All-Wise) are singled out for mention. Why?\nلَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٣ ءَايَٰتٞ لِّقَوۡمٖ يُوقِنُونَ ٤ ءَايَٰتٞ لِّقَوۡمٖ يَعۡقِلُونَ ٥\nAllah said first: (Signs for the believers), then, (Signs for people who are certain in faith), then, (Signs for people who reason), thus ascending from one honorable stage to what is more honorable and higher rank. Ibn Kathir: 4/150.\nDescribing the believers in this order: Believers, certain in faith, and those who reason. Why?\nإِنَّ فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ لَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٣ وَفِي خَلۡقِكُمۡ وَمَا يَبُثُّ مِن دَآبَّةٍ ءَايَٰتٞ لِّقَوۡمٖ يُوقِنُونَ ٤ وَٱخۡتِلَٰفِ ٱلَّيۡلِ وَٱلنَّهَارِ وَمَآ أَنزَلَ ٱللَّهُ مِنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ مِن رِّزۡقٖ فَأَحۡيَا بِهِ ٱلۡأَرۡضَ بَعۡدَ مَوۡتِهَا وَتَصۡرِيفِ ٱلرِّيَٰحِ ءَايَٰتٞ لِّقَوۡمٖ يَعۡقِلُونَ ٥\nSix proofs of the Oneness of Allah, which point to His Might, Sublimity, absolute Power, and the fact that He alone is worthy of worship. First: His creation of the heavens and earth. Second: His creation of mankind. Third: His creation of moving creatures. Fourth: The alternation of the night and day. Fifth: Sending the rain from the sky and reviving the earth. Sixth: Directing of the winds. Al-Shanqiti: 7/179.\nIn these verses, Allah mentions six proofs of His Might and Sublimity. What are they?\nوَمَآ أَنزَلَ ٱللَّهُ مِنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ مِن رِّزۡقٖ فَأَحۡيَا بِهِ ٱلۡأَرۡضَ بَعۡدَ مَوۡتِهَا\nAllah, the Almighty, sends down the rain from the clouds when it is most needed. He is calling the rain, a \"provision\", because it is the main resource that helps produce provisions. Ibn Kathir: 4/150.\nAllah calls the rain: A \"provision.\" Why?\nوَيۡلٞ لِّكُلِّ أَفَّاكٍ أَثِيمٖ ٧ يَسۡمَعُ ءَايَٰتِ ٱللَّهِ تُتۡلَىٰ عَلَيۡهِ ثُمَّ يُصِرُّ مُسۡتَكۡبِرٗا كَأَن لَّمۡ يَسۡمَعۡهَاۖ فَبَشِّرۡهُ بِعَذَابٍ أَلِيمٖ ٨\nFrom these verses, it is clear that whoever turns away in arrogance from the verses of Allah, is an excessive sinner and a liar, hence he deserves a painful punishment. Al-Biqai: 7/93.\nWhat is the fate of one who does not respond to the guidance of the Quran?\nمِّن وَرَآئِهِمۡ جَهَنَّمُۖ وَلَا يُغۡنِي عَنۡهُم مَّا كَسَبُواْ شَيۡـٔٗا وَلَا مَا ٱتَّخَذُواْ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ أَوۡلِيَآءَۖ\n(Behind them is Hell): In describing what will happen to them in the future, the word, (behind) is used to depict their turning away from the Fire as if it were behind them. Al-Shawkani: 5/5.\nThe word, (behind) is used to denote the future. Why?\nإِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّقَوۡمٖ يَتَفَكَّرُونَ ١٣\nWhen mentioning those who are guided by the signs, those who reflect are mentioned last, because reflection is the essence of belief, certainty, and knowledge, which are mentioned in: (Signs for the believers) , (Signs for people who are certain in faith) , (Signs for people who reason). Ibn Ashur: 25/338.\nShow the benefit of reflection.\nwords\nيَبُثُّHe disperses\nوَيلٌWoe\nأَفَّاكٍLiar\nأَثِيمٍSinful\nهُزُوًاRidicule"],[500,"§Al-Jathiyah\ndeeds\nSupplicate Allah to make knowledge a reason for your guidance and righteousness and not a reason for your misguidance and deviation.\nPerform the required and optional ordinances with the intention of following Sharia, even if they go against your desires.\nWrite an article or a message in which you emphasize the importance of adhering to Sharia as a complete way of life.\nguid\nCheck your heart, and if there is an envy in it toward anyone, pray for them and ask forgiveness for them.\nAny statement that contradicts the Quran and Sunnah can only emanate from whims, of which Allah has prohibited to follow.\nAllah has established a connection between whims and lack of knowledge; whoever is ignorant, is closer to following his whims.\nrefl\nمَنۡ عَمِلَ صَٰلِحٗا فَلِنَفۡسِهِۦۖ وَمَنۡ أَسَآءَ فَعَلَيۡهَاۖ ثُمَّ إِلَىٰ رَبِّكُمۡ تُرۡجَعُونَ ١٥\nAny servant who does righteous deeds, follows Allah's commands, and observes His prohibitions, it is for his own benefit that he performed these righteous deeds, seeking salvation for his soul from Allah’s punishment. He obeyed his Lord for nothing other than that, and his deeds will not benefit anyone else but him, since Allah is in no need of the deeds of anyone. (And whoever does an evil deed, it is to his own loss), whoever does evil in worldly life by disobeying Allah, disregarding His commands and prohibitions, it is to his own loss because he ruined himself, deserved Allah’s wrath, and harmed no one but himself. Al-Tabari: 22/68.\nAllah links the good deeds and evil ones to the one who performs them. Why?\nوَلَقَدۡ ءَاتَيۡنَا بَنِيٓ إِسۡرَٰٓءِيلَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ وَٱلۡحُكۡمَ وَٱلنُّبُوَّةَ وَرَزَقۡنَٰهُم مِّنَ ٱلطَّيِّبَٰتِ وَفَضَّلۡنَٰهُمۡ عَلَى ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ١٦ وَءَاتَيۡنَٰهُم بَيِّنَٰتٖ مِّنَ ٱلۡأَمۡرِۖ فَمَا ٱخۡتَلَفُوٓاْ إِلَّا مِنۢ بَعۡدِ مَا جَآءَهُمُ ٱلۡعِلۡمُ بَغۡيَۢا بَيۡنَهُمۡۚ إِنَّ رَبَّكَ يَقۡضِي بَيۡنَهُمۡ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِ فِيمَا كَانُواْ فِيهِ يَخۡتَلِفُونَ ١٧\nThis verse contains a warning to the Muslim Ummah as well. It warns them not to take the path the Jews took nor adopt their ways. Ibn Kathir: 4/152.\nWhat lesson should we, Muslims, learn from these two verses about the Children of Israel?\nوَفَضَّلۡنَٰهُمۡ عَلَى ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ١٦\nEvery mention of favoring the Children of Israel in the Quran refers to the past, because they denied and rejected the Quran at the time of its revelation, as Allah says, (But when there came to them what they recognize [to be true], they rejected it. May the curse of Allah be upon the disbelievers) [2:89]. It is well known that Allah did not mention favoring them except with regard to the past, and not during the revelation of the Quran. Al-Shanqiti: 7/198-199.\nExplain the favoring of the Children of Israel above all others.\nفَمَا ٱخۡتَلَفُوٓاْ إِلَّا مِنۢ بَعۡدِ مَا جَآءَهُمُ ٱلۡعِلۡمُ بَغۡيَۢا بَيۡنَهُمۡۚ\nMeaning: Envying the Prophet (ﷺ). It is said that (transgression), they wronged each other over worldly glory and headship. Moreover, they have killed their Prophets. Similarly, when the clear directions in matters of religion came to the polytheists of your time, O Muhammad, they turned away to rival in headship. Al-Qurtubi: 19/153.\nWhat was the transgression they did?\nثُمَّ جَعَلۡنَٰكَ عَلَىٰ شَرِيعَةٖ مِّنَ ٱلۡأَمۡرِ فَٱتَّبِعۡهَا\nAllah said that He had put the Children of Israel on a clear way of the religion, and warned them not to differ about it, thus, it became a warning to us also as Allah declares the superiority of our Sharia, and says, (Then We put you [O Prophet] on a clear way of the religion; so follow it). Al-Biqai: 7/100.\nWhat is the link between this verse (Then We put you [O Prophet] on a clear way of the religion) and the previous verses?\nهَٰذَا بَصَٰٓئِرُ لِلنَّاسِ وَهُدٗى وَرَحۡمَةٞ لِّقَوۡمٖ يُوقِنُونَ ٢٠\nAllah singles out those who are certain in faith with an insight, a guidance and mercy, because they are the ones who benefited from the Quran, and not the disbelievers who denied it, thus, it is upon them blindness and sorrow. Al-Tabari: 22/72.\nAllah made the Quran an insight, a guidance and mercy for people who are certain in faith. Why?\nأَمۡ حَسِبَ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱجۡتَرَحُواْ ٱلسَّيِّـَٔاتِ أَن نَّجۡعَلَهُمۡ كَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ سَوَآءٗ مَّحۡيَاهُمۡ وَمَمَاتُهُمۡۚ سَآءَ مَا يَحۡكُمُونَ ٢١\nIbrahim bin Al-Ash'ath said: I often saw Fudhail bin Iyadh repeating this verse and similar verses to it throughout the night; then he used to say: I wonder, among which group will I be? Moreover, this verse has a weeping effect on worshipers. Al-Qurtubi: 19/157.\nHow did the righteous predecessors interact with this verse?\nwords\nلاَ يَرجُونَ أَيَّامَ اللهِThey do not expect Allah's retribution\nوَالحُكمَJudgment\nلَن يُغنُوا عَنكَThey will never avail you\nبَصَائِرُEnlightenment for guiding people"]])